pt":"Ferramenta Context-Hunter: Colaboração de Projetos com Fe...","ru":"ИИ Агент Context-Hunter: Управление Проектами в Git","ar":"أداة Context-Hunter: إدارة مشاريع التعاون بين البشر ووكلا...","en":"context-hunter"},"description":{"zh":"Context-Hunter是一种用于管理Git项目协作的工具，实现人类和AI智能工具之间的合作","ja":"Context-Hunterは、Gitプロジェクトのコラボレーションを管理するためのツールで、人間とAIエージェントの間で共同作業を行う","ko":"Context-Hunter는 Git 프로젝트 협업을 관리하는 도구로서 인간과 AI 에이전트 간의 협력을 thực現","es":"Context-hunter es una herramienta para la gestión de la colaboración de proyectos entre humanos y Agentes de IA en un ecosistema git","fr":"Context-hunter est un outil pour la gestion de la collaboration de projets entre humains et Agents d''IA dans un écosystème git","de":"Context-hunter ist ein Tool für die Verwaltung der Projektzusammenarbeit zwischen Menschen und KI-Agents in einem Git-Ökosystem","pt":"Context-Hunter é uma ferramenta para gerenciar projetos em colaboração com Ferramentas de IA no ecossistema Git. Ela permite uma gestão eficaz de projetos.","ru":"ИИ Агент Context-Hunter - это инструмент для управления проектами в Git с помощью инструментов искусственного интеллекта. Он обеспечивает эффективное управле...","ar":"أداة Context-Hunter هي أداة لإدارة مشاريع التعاون بين البشر ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي في بيئة جيت. إنها تمكن الإدارة الفعالة للمشاريع.","en":"Backlog.md - A tool for managing project collaboration between humans and AI Agents in a git ecosystem"},"definition":{"en":"Backlog.md - A tool for managing project collaboration between humans and AI Agents in a git ecosystem"},"features":{"zh":["支持Git项目协作","实现人类和AI智能工具之间的合作","提高项目协作效率","支持多种编程语言","提供CLI接口"],"ja":["Gitプロジェクトのコラボレーションをサポート","人間とAIエージェントの間で共同作業を実現","プロジェクトのコラボレーション効率を向上","複数のプログラミング言語をサポート","CLIインターフェースを提供"],"ko":["Git 프로젝트 협업을 지원","인간과 AI 에이전트 간의 협력을 实现","프로젝트 협업 효율성을 높임","다양한 프로그래밍 언어를 지원","CLI 인터페이스를 제공"],"es":["Gestión de proyectos en un ecosistema git","Colaboración entre humanos y Agentes de IA","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo","Seguimiento de progreso y控制 de versiones","Soporte para múltiples lenguajes de programación"],"fr":["Gestion de projets dans un écosystème git","Collaboration entre humains et Agents d''IA","Intégration avec des outils de développement","Suivi de progression et contrôle de versions","Prise en charge de plusieurs langages de programmation"],"de":["Projektmanagement in einem Git-Ökosystem","Zusammenarbeit zwischen Menschen und KI-Agents","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Verfolgung von Fortschritten und Versionskontrolle","Unterstützung für mehrere Programmiersprachen"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de projetos em colaboração com Ferramentas de IA","Integração com o ecossistema Git","Gestão eficaz de projetos","Colaboração entre humanos e Ferramentas de IA","Suporte a múltiplos projetos"],"ru":["Управление проектами в сотрудничестве с ИИ Агентами","Интеграция с экосистемой Git","Эффективное управление проектами","Совместная работа людей и ИИ Агентов","Поддержка нескольких проектов"],"ar":["إدارة مشاريع التعاون بين البشر ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع بيئة جيت","الإدارة الفعالة للمشاريع","التعاون بين البشر ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","دعم مشاريع متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Context-Hunter","AI智能工具","Git项目协作","如何使用Context-Hunter","Context-Hunter安装","Context-Hunter替代品"],"ja":["Context-Hunter","AIエージェント","Gitプロジェクトコラボレーション","Context-Hunterの使い方","Context-Hunterのインストール","Context-Hunterの代替"],"ko":["Context-Hunter","AI 에이전트","Git 프로젝트 협업","Context-Hunter 사용법","Context-Hunter 설치","Context-Hunter 대체"],"es":["cómo usar context-hunter","qué es un Agente de IA","alternativas a context-hunter","context-hunter vs Jira","instalación de context-hunter","guía de configuración de context-hunter","desarrollo de proyectos con Agentes de IA"],"fr":["comment utiliser context-hunter","qu''est-ce qu''un Agent d''IA","alternatives à context-hunter","context-hunter vs Jira","installation de context-hunter","guide de configuration de context-hunter","développement de projets avec des Agents d''IA"],"de":["wie man context-hunter verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","alternativen zu context-hunter","context-hunter vs Jira","installation von context-hunter","konfigurationsanleitung für context-hunter","projektentwicklung mit KI-Agents"],"pt":["como usar Context-Hunter","o que é Context-Hunter","Context-Hunter alternativa","Context-Hunter vs Jira","instalar Context-Hunter","guia de configuração do Context-Hunter","ferramentas de IA para gestão de projetos"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агент Context-Hunter","что такое ИИ Агент Context-Hunter","ИИ Агент Context-Hunter альтернатива","ИИ Агент Context-Hunter vs Jira","установить ИИ Агент Context-Hunter","руководство по настройке ИИ Агента Context-Hunter","инструменты ИИ для управления проектами"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة Context-Hunter","ما هي أداة Context-Hunter","أداة Context-Hunter بديلة","أداة Context-Hunter مقابل Jira","تثبيت أداة Context-Hunter","دليل إعداد أداة Context-Hunter","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لإدارة المشاريع"]}},"owner":"MrLesk","repo":"Backlog.md","repoPath":"MrLesk/Backlog.md","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.962Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"context-hunter","description":"MUST run before any code implementation task. Classifies complexity, discovers local conventions, finds reusable patterns, and prevents blind coding. Invoke this skill before writing or modifying code.","bodyPreview":"# Context Hunter\n\nBefore writing code, run a focused discovery loop.\nDo not load everything. Find the right files.\n\n## Complexity Gate\n\nClassify task complexity first:\n\n- `L0 (trivial)`: typos, renames, copy-only edits, obvious single-line fixes with no behavior change.\n- `L1 (moderate)`: behavior changes in one bounded area.\n- `L2 (high-risk)`: cross-module changes, data semantics, refactors, architecture-impacting work.\n\nOutput by level:\n- `L0`: no context brief, proceed directly.\n- `L1`: writ","body":"# Context Hunter\n\nBefore writing code, run a focused discovery loop.\nDo not load everything. Find the right files.\n\n## Complexity Gate\n\nClassify task complexity first:\n\n- `L0 (trivial)`: typos, renames, copy-only edits, obvious single-line fixes with no behavior change.\n- `L1 (moderate)`: behavior changes in one bounded area.\n- `L2 (high-risk)`: cross-module changes, data semantics, refactors, architecture-impacting work.\n\nOutput by level:\n- `L0`: no context brief, proceed directly.\n- `L1`: write a micro-brief.\n- `L2`: write a full context brief.\n\nRe-evaluate level during discovery and implementation.\nIf new evidence shows higher complexity than initially classified, upgrade the level and apply the stricter workflow.\n\n## Core Behavior\n\nAct like a senior engineer who asks the next useful question:\n1. **Assess completeness**: Check whether the request omits expected concerns seen in analogous code.\n2. **Discover selectively**: Read the minimum set of relevant files.\n3. **Validate assumptions**: Confirm with tests/config/history.\n4. **Synthesize**: Capture findings before coding for `L1/L2`.\n\n## Discovery Workflow (Before Coding)\n\n### 1) Assess Request Completeness\n\nAsk: \"What is likely missing?\"\n\nExamples:\n- Similar endpoints include auth/validation. Is that expected here?\n- This area uses soft-delete semantics. Should this operation follow that?\n- Similar flows emit telemetry/error states. Should this change do the same?\n- Existing module boundaries suggest a different placement. Is current request still correct?\n\n### 2) Run Targeted Discovery\n\nPrioritize these in order:\n1. Find analogous implementations and copy their structure.\n2. Trace data flow for similar features end-to-end.\n3. Identify reusable utilities before creating new helpers.\n4. Inspect nearby tests to infer team priorities and edge cases.\n5. Read recent commits in the same area for current direction.\n\nPortable discovery actions:\n- Search for feature/domain terms in relevant directories.\n- Enumerate nearby files in the affected area.\n- Inspect recent change history for touched paths.\n- Run targeted validation first, then broader project checks as needed.\n\n### 3) Probe for Silent Knowledge\n\nLook for implicit rules encoded in code:\n- Soft-delete, audit, or historical retention patterns (for data-touching changes).\n- Naming conventions (`userId` vs `user_id`) and file placement norms.\n- Existing design system choices (for this repo: Nuxt + Vue + Tailwind 4.1 patterns).\n- “Dead but dangerous” APIs/functions that exist but are no longer preferred.\n\n### 4) Confidence-Based Stop Rule\n\nStop discovery when confidence is high enough to predict likely review feedback.\nIf you cannot anticipate reviewer concerns yet, keep looking.\n\n### 5) Produce Scaled Discovery Output\n\nFor `L1`, write a micro-brief:\n- Closest analog and chosen pattern.\n- Main risk or ambiguity.\n\nFor `L2`, write a full context brief:\n- Analogous files reviewed (with paths).\n- Patterns to follow (state/data/error handling/naming).\n- Reusable utilities/components/composables identified.\n- Risks and unknowns.\n\nFor `L1/L2`, keep an internal discovery log:\n- Files checked.\n- Patterns inferred.\n- Decisions made from evidence.\n- Naming evidence for new identifiers (`new name -> analog paths -> extracted pattern`).\n\n## Clarification Policy\n\n- Prefer fewer questions.\n- Ask only when the answer would change implementation approach.\n- If convention is clear, proceed silently.\n- Escalate only genuine ambiguity/conflict or product-level tradeoffs.\n\n## During Implementation\n\nChanges should look native to the codebase:\n- Reuse existing abstractions first.\n- Match existing module boundaries and naming.\n- Follow established error-handling and testing style.\n- Prefer consistency over novelty.\n\nNaming derivation rule:\n- Do not invent names from general priors.\n- For each new identifier family (file/function/variable/class/route), derive naming from closest local analogs.\n- Use at least 2 analogous examples when available before finalizing a new naming pattern.\n- If no analog exists, introduce the new term explicitly and record it as a no-analog exception.\n\nIf requirements conflict with discovered conventions:\n- Flag the conflict explicitly.\n- Propose 1-2 alternatives aligned with existing patterns.\n- Ask for decision when tradeoffs are product/architecture-level.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter coding:\n- Run targeted validation for changed area first.\n- Run broader checks appropriate for risk (`typecheck`, lint/check, tests as needed).\n- Confirm no new pattern drift was introduced.\n\n## Checklist\n\n`L0`:\n- [ ] Confirmed change is truly trivial and safe to execute without full discovery.\n\n`L1/L2`:\n- [ ] Classified complexity (`L0/L1/L2`) before discovery\n- [ ] Studied analogous features in the codebase\n- [ ] Checked for reusable utilities\n- [ ] Reviewed test patterns for similar functionality\n- [ ] Assessed request completeness before implementation\n- [ ] Identified at least one silent convention/risk\n- [ ] Produced the required artifact for the chosen level\n- [ ] Kept an internal discovery log for `L1/L2`\n- [ ] All new names were derived from codebase analogs, or marked as intentional no-analog exceptions\n- [ ] Verified final approach matches existing patterns\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:49:59.332Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing efficient task complexity classification and context discovery","zh":"非常适合需要高效任务复杂性分类和上下文发现的代码审查代理","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが効率的なタスクの複雑さの分類とコンテキストの発見を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트가 효율적인 작업 복잡도 분류 및 컨텍스트 발견을 필요로 할 때 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan una clasificación eficiente de la complejidad de las tareas y el descubrimiento de contexto","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant une classification efficace de la complexité des tâches et la découverte de contexte","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die eine effiziente Aufgabenkomplexitätsklassifizierung und Kontextentdeckung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de classificação eficiente de complexidade de tarefas e descoberta de contexto","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов код-ревью, которым требуется эффективная классификация сложности задач и обнаружение контекста","ar":"مثالي لعميل استعراض الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى تصنيف كفء لتعقيد المهمة واكتشاف السياق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to classify task complexity using levels L0, L1, and L2, and provides focused discovery loops to find the right files, streamlining collaboration in git ecosystems with tools like Backlog.md","zh":"赋予代理使用级别L0、L1和L2对任务复杂性进行分类的能力，并提供专注的发现循环来找到正确的文件，从而在使用Backlog.md等工具的git生态系统中简化协作","ja":"エージェントにタスクの複雑さをL0、L1、L2のレベルで分類する能力を与え、Backlog.mdなどのツールを使用するgitエコシステムでのコラボレーションを簡素化するために、正しいファイルを見つけるための集中した検出ループを提供する","ko":"에이전트에게 작업 복잡도를 수준 L0, L1, L2로 분류할 수 있는 능력을 부여하고 Backlog.md와 같은 도구를 사용하는 git 생태계에서 협업을 간소화하기 위해 올바른 파일을 찾는 집중된 검색 루프를 제공함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a clasificar la complejidad de las tareas utilizando los niveles L0, L1 y L2, y proporciona bucles de descubrimiento enfocados para encontrar los archivos adecuados, simplificando la colaboración en ecosistemas git con herramientas como Backlog.md","fr":"Permet aux agents de classer la complexité des tâches en utilisant les niveaux L0, L1 et L2, et fournit des boucles de découverte ciblées pour trouver les fichiers appropriés, simplifiant la collaboration dans les écosystèmes git avec des outils comme Backlog.md","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Aufgabenkomplexität mit den Ebenen L0, L1 und L2 zu klassifizieren und bietet fokussierte Entdeckungsschleifen, um die richtigen Dateien zu finden, wodurch die Zusammenarbeit in git-Ökosystemen mit Tools wie Backlog.md optimiert wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a classificar a complexidade das tarefas usando níveis L0, L1 e L2, e fornece loops de descoberta focados para encontrar os arquivos certos, otimizando a colaboração em ecossistemas git com ferramentas como Backlog.md","ru":"Позволяет агентам классифицировать сложность задач на уровнях L0, L1 и L2 и предоставляет сосредоточенные циклы обнаружения для нахождения нужных файлов, оптимизируя сотрудничество в экосистемах git с помощью инструментов типа Backlog.md","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تصنيف تعقيد المهمة باستخدام مستويات L0 و L1 و L2، ويقدم حلقات اكتشاف محددة لايجاد الملفات الصحيحة، ويعزز التعاون في بيئات جيت باستخدام أدوات مثل Backlog.md"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating task complexity assessment","Streamlining code reviews with targeted context briefs","Optimizing collaboration workflows in git ecosystems"],"zh":["自动化任务复杂性评估","使用有针对性的上下文简报来简化代码审查","在git生态系统中优化协作工作流"],"ja":["タスクの複雑さの評価を自動化する","ターゲットを絞ったコンテキストブリーフを使用してコードレビューを簡素化する","gitエコシステムでのコラボレーションワークフローを最適化する"],"ko":["작업 복잡도 평가 자동화","타겟을 좁힌 컨텍스트 브리핑을 사용하여 코드 리뷰를 간소화","git 생태계에서 협업 워크플로우를 최적화"],"es":["Automatización de la evaluación de la complejidad de las tareas","Optimización de las revisiones de código con informes de contexto dirigidos","Optimización de los flujos de trabajo de colaboración en ecosistemas git"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''évaluation de la complexité des tâches","Optimisation des révisions de code avec des rapports de contexte ciblés","Optimisation des flux de travail de collaboration dans les écosystèmes git"],"de":["Automatisierung der Bewertung der Aufgabenkomplexität","Optimierung der Code-Reviews mit gezielten Kontextberichten","Optimierung der Zusammenarbeitsprozesse in git-Ökosystemen"],"pt":["Automatizar a avaliação da complexidade das tarefas","Otimizar as revisões de código com breves contextos direcionados","Otimizar os fluxos de trabalho de colaboração em ecossistemas git"],"ru":["Автоматизировать оценку сложности задач","Оптимизировать код-ревью с помощью целевых контекстных заметок","Оптимизировать рабочие процессы сотрудничества в экосистемах git"],"ar":["أتمتة تقييم تعقيد المهام","تحسين استعراض الشفرة مع ملخصات سياق مستهدفة","تحسين سير عمل التعاون في بيئات جيت"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git ecosystem integration","Limited to classification levels L0, L1, and L2"],"zh":["需要git生态系统集成","仅限于L0、L1和L2的分类级别"],"ja":["gitエコシステムの統合が必要","分類レベルはL0、L1、L2に限定"],"ko":["git 생태계 통합이 필요","분류 수준은 L0, L1, L2로 제한"],"es":["Requiere integración con el ecosistema git","Limitado a los niveles de clasificación L0, L1 y L2"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec l''écosystème git","Limité aux niveaux de classification L0, L1 et L2"],"de":["Erfordert Integration in das git-Ökosystem","Begrenzt auf die Klassifizierungsstufen L0, L1 und L2"],"pt":["Requer integração com ecossistema git","Limitado a níveis de classificação L0, L1 e L2"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с экосистемой git","Ограничен уровнями классификации L0, L1 и L2"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع بيئة جيت","محدود بمستويات التصنيف L0 و L1 و L2"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"8f634b3adef2d8f691d96827da4ade9e4ba7d332bd9a4d892560fe56893da8b0","qualityScore":29}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hack-dance/hack/hack-cli', 'community', 'hack-dance', 'hack', 'hack-dance/hack', 'hack-cli', 0, 0, 29, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.999Z', '2026-03-02T03:05:22.423Z', '14aa38fb0747528de111e45fd1d094729ec60bcf46a445aebca3597e17a6e8b0', '{"id":"hack-dance/hack/hack-cli","name":"hack-cli","description":{"zh":"hack-cli 是一个本地开发编排工具，用于运行多个项目同时避免端口冲突","ja":"hack-cli は、複数のプロジェクトを同時に実行しながらポートコンフリクトを回避するローカル開発オーケストレーションツール","ko":"hack-cli는 포트 충돌 없이 여러 프로젝트를同時에 실행하는 로컬 개발 오케스트레이션 도구","es":"Hack-cli es una herramienta de orquestación local para ejecutar múltiples proyectos al mismo tiempo sin conflictos de puertos","fr":"Hack-cli est un outil d''orchestration local pour exécuter plusieurs projets en même temps sans conflits de ports","de":"Hack-cli ist ein lokales Orchestrierungstool, um mehrere Projekte gleichzeitig ohne Portkonflikte auszuführen","pt":"O hack-cli é uma ferramenta de orquestração de desenvolvimento local que permite executar vários projetos ao mesmo tempo sem conflitos de portas.","ru":"ИИ Агент hack-cli - это инструмент для местной разработки, позволяющий запускать несколько проектов одновременно без конфликтов портов.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي hack-cli هي أداة أوركسترا التطوير المحلي التي تسمح بتشغيل عدة مشاريع في نفس الوقت دون صراعات المنافذ.","en":"Opinionated local-dev orchestration for running multiple projects at the same time without port conflicts."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AIエージェント hack-cli：本地开发编排","ja":"AIエージェント hack-cli：ローカル開発オーケストレーション","ko":"AI 에이전트 hack-cli: 로컬 개발 오케스트레이션","es":"Herramientas AI: hack-cli para desarrollo local","fr":"Outils IA: hack-cli pour le développement local","de":"KI-Tools: hack-cli für lokale Entwicklung","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: hack-cli para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: hack-cli для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: hack-cli لل مطورين","en":"hack-cli"},"description":{"zh":"hack-cli 是一个本地开发编排工具，用于运行多个项目同时避免端口冲突","ja":"hack-cli は、複数のプロジェクトを同時に実行しながらポートコンフリクトを回避するローカル開発オーケストレーションツール","ko":"hack-cli는 포트 충돌 없이 여러 프로젝트를同時에 실행하는 로컬 개발 오케스트레이션 도구","es":"Hack-cli es una herramienta de orquestación local para ejecutar múltiples proyectos al mismo tiempo sin conflictos de puertos","fr":"Hack-cli est un outil d''orchestration local pour exécuter plusieurs projets en même temps sans conflits de ports","de":"Hack-cli ist ein lokales Orchestrierungstool, um mehrere Projekte gleichzeitig ohne Portkonflikte auszuführen","pt":"O hack-cli é uma ferramenta de orquestração de desenvolvimento local que permite executar vários projetos ao mesmo tempo sem conflitos de portas.","ru":"ИИ Агент hack-cli - это инструмент для местной разработки, позволяющий запускать несколько проектов одновременно без конфликтов портов.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي hack-cli هي أداة أوركسترا التطوير المحلي التي تسمح بتشغيل عدة مشاريع في نفس الوقت دون صراعات المنافذ.","en":"Opinionated local-dev orchestration for running multiple projects at the same time without port conflicts."},"definition":{"en":"Opinionated local-dev orchestration for running multiple projects at the same time without port conflicts."},"features":{"zh":["无端口冲突的多项目开发","本地开发编排","CLI 工具","支持多个项目同时运行","提高开发效率"],"ja":["ポートコンフリクトのないマルチプロジェクト開発","ローカル開発オーケストレーション","CLI ツール","複数のプロジェクトを同時に実行","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["포트 충돌 없는 멀티 프로젝트 개발","로컬 개발 오케스트레이션","CLI 도구","여러 프로젝트를同時에 실행","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Orquestación de proyectos locales","Evita conflictos de puertos","Ejecución de múltiples proyectos al mismo tiempo","Interfaz de línea de comandos (CLI)","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo locales"],"fr":["Orchestration de projets locaux","Évite les conflits de ports","Exécution de plusieurs projets en même temps","Interface de ligne de commande (CLI)","Intégration avec des outils de développement locaux"],"de":["Orchestrierung lokaler Projekte","Vermeidung von Portkonflikten","Ausführung mehrerer Projekte gleichzeitig","Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle (CLI)","Integration mit lokalen Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Execução de vários projetos simultaneamente","Evita conflitos de portas","Orquestração de desenvolvimento local","Fácil de usar","Suporte a múltiplos projetos"],"ru":["Запуск нескольких проектов одновременно","Избегает конфликтов портов","Местная разработка","Легко использовать","Поддержка нескольких проектов"],"ar":["تشغيل عدة مشاريع في نفس الوقت","تتجنب صراعات المنافذ","أوركسترا التطوير المحلي","سهلة الاستخدام","دعم عدة مشاريع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["hack-cli 安装","本地开发编排工具","多项目开发解决方案","如何使用 hack-cli","hack-cli 与其他工具的比较","hack-cli 教程","CLI 工具开发","本地开发效率提高"],"ja":["hack-cli インストール","ローカル開発オーケストレーションツール","マルチプロジェクト開発ソリューション","hack-cli の使用方法","hack-cli と他のツールの比較","hack-cli チュートリアル","CLI ツール開発","ローカル開発効率の向上"],"ko":["hack-cli 설치","로컬 개발 오케스트레이션 도구","멀티 프로젝트 개발 솔루션","hack-cli 사용법","hack-cli와 다른 도구의 비교","hack-cli 튜토리얼","CLI 도구 개발","로컬 개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["herramientas AI para desarrollo local","hack-cli alternative","cómo usar hack-cli","orquestación de proyectos locales","evitar conflictos de puertos","instalación de hack-cli","guía de configuración de hack-cli"],"fr":["outils IA pour le développement local","alternative à hack-cli","comment utiliser hack-cli","orchestration de projets locaux","éviter les conflits de ports","installation de hack-cli","guide de configuration de hack-cli"],"de":["KI-Tools für lokale Entwicklung","Alternative zu hack-cli","wie man hack-cli verwendet","Orchestrierung lokaler Projekte","Vermeidung von Portkonflikten","Installation von hack-cli","Konfigurationsanleitung für hack-cli"],"pt":["como usar hack-cli","o que é hack-cli","hack-cli alternativa","hack-cli vs docker","instalar hack-cli","guia de configuração do hack-cli"],"ru":["как использовать hack-cli","что такое hack-cli","hack-cli альтернатива","hack-cli vs docker","установить hack-cli","руководство по настройке hack-cli"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام hack-cli","ما هي hack-cli","بديل hack-cli","hack-cli مقابل دッカー","تثبيت hack-cli","دليل إعداد hack-cli"]}},"owner":"hack-dance","repo":"hack","repoPath":"hack-dance/hack","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.999Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"hack-cli","description":">","bodyPreview":"# hack CLI\n\nUse `hack` as the primary interface for local development.\n\n## Operating Rules\n\n- Prefer `hack` over raw `docker` / `docker compose`.\n- Do not start/stop project services from Docker Desktop UI for `hack`-managed repos.\n- Treat `.hack/.internal` and `.hack/.branch` as hack-managed artifacts; avoid hand-editing generated files.\n- Use MCP only when shell access is unavailable.\n- Run `hack doctor` (and `hack doctor --fix`) before manual runtime/network repair.\n\n## Config + Schema\n\n- Pro","body":"# hack CLI\n\nUse `hack` as the primary interface for local development.\n\n## Operating Rules\n\n- Prefer `hack` over raw `docker` / `docker compose`.\n- Do not start/stop project services from Docker Desktop UI for `hack`-managed repos.\n- Treat `.hack/.internal` and `.hack/.branch` as hack-managed artifacts; avoid hand-editing generated files.\n- Use MCP only when shell access is unavailable.\n- Run `hack doctor` (and `hack doctor --fix`) before manual runtime/network repair.\n\n## Config + Schema\n\n- Project config: `.hack/hack.config.json`\n- Global config: `~/.hack/hack.config.json`\n- Schema URL: `https://schemas.hack/hack.config.schema.json`\n- Prefer CLI config edits via `hack config get/set`.\n\n## Hostname Routing\n\n- Primary host is `dev_host` (default: `<project>.hack`).\n- Subdomains use `<sub>.<dev_host>` (for example: `api.myapp.hack`).\n- OAuth alias can add `<dev_host>.<tld>` and `<sub>.<dev_host>.<tld>` (default: `gy`).\n- Only HTTP services with Caddy labels and `hack-dev` network attachment are routable.\n- Required labels: `caddy`, `caddy.reverse_proxy`, `caddy.tls=internal`.\n- Quick checks: `hack open`, `hack open <sub>`, `hack open --json`.\n\n## TLS + OAuth Host Rules\n\n- Caddy internal PKI provides HTTPS for routed hosts; trust CA with `hack global trust`.\n- `.hack` is local-first and not a public suffix.\n- Use alias hosts like `*.hack.gy` when provider callback validation rejects non-public-suffix hosts.\n- Alias hosts are local routes unless you explicitly add remote ingress/tunnel plumbing.\n\n## Managed Files\n\n- Source-of-truth files: `.hack/docker-compose.yml`, `.hack/hack.config.json`, `.hack/hack.env.json`.\n- Local-only files: `.hack/.env` and `.hack/.internal/` (gitignored; machine-specific state).\n- Generated by hack: `.hack/.internal/compose.override.yml`, `.hack/.internal/compose.env.override.yml`, `.hack/.branch/compose.<branch>.override.yml`.\n- Managed via CLI: `.hack/.internal/extra-hosts.json` using `hack internal extra-hosts ...` commands.\n- Lifecycle runtime files: `.hack/.internal/lifecycle/state.json`, `.hack/.internal/lifecycle/*.log`.\n\n## Advanced Networking\n\n- Static host mappings: set `internal.extra_hosts` in `.hack/hack.config.json`.\n- Dynamic mappings for local proxies/tunnels: `hack internal extra-hosts set <hostname> <target>`.\n- List/remove mappings: `hack internal extra-hosts list` / `hack internal extra-hosts unset <hostname>`.\n- Prefer `host-gateway` for host-local proxy targets when possible.\n- Apply changes with `hack restart`; verify with `hack doctor`.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n- Bootstrap project config: `hack init`\n- Start services: `hack up --detach`\n- Alternate shorthand: `hack up -d`\n- Restart services: `hack restart`\n- Open app: `hack open --json`\n- Tail logs (compose): `hack logs --pretty`\n- Per-service logs: `hack logs <service>`\n- Snapshot logs: `hack logs --json --no-follow`\n- Loki history/query: `hack logs --loki --since 2h --pretty`\n- Run commands: `hack run <service> <cmd...>`\n- Stop services: `hack down`\n\n## Global Infra\n\n- Install once: `hack global install`\n- Start/stop/status: `hack global up`, `hack global down`, `hack global status`\n- Global logs: `hack global logs <service> --no-follow --tail 200`\n\n## Remote Nodes + Dispatch\n\n- Pair/register a node: `hack node pair ...`, then verify via `hack node list` and `hack node status --watch`.\n- Repair SSH access for remote Git/mutagen: `hack node ssh setup --node <id>`.\n- Inspect node workspace map on the node host: `ssh <user@host> ''hack node workspace list --json''`.\n- Inspect/repair controller route bridge: `hack node routes status`, `hack node routes repair`.\n- Dispatch command to remote workspace: `hack dispatch run --project <name|id> --node default --branch <branch> --runner generic -- \"pwd\"`.\n\n## Lifecycle + Startup\n\n- Put host setup in `.hack/hack.config.json` under `startup` / `lifecycle`.\n- Use lifecycle processes for long-running host tasks, not ad-hoc terminals.\n- Inspect via `hack projects --details` and `hack logs <service-or-process>`.\n\n## Branch Instances\n\nUse branch instances to run parallel environments:\n\n- `hack up --branch <name> --detach`\n- `hack open --branch <name>`\n- `hack logs --branch <name>`\n- `hack down --branch <name>`\n\n## Sessions\n\n- Picker: `hack session`\n- Start/attach: `hack session start <project>`\n- Isolated agent session: `hack session start <project> --new --name agent-1`\n- Exec: `hack session exec <session> \"<command>\"`\n- Stop: `hack session stop <session>`\n\n## Tickets\n\n- Create: `hack tickets create --title \"...\" --body-stdin`\n- List/show: `hack tickets list`, `hack tickets show T-00001`\n- Status/sync: `hack tickets status T-00001 in_progress`, `hack tickets sync`\n\n## Project Targeting\n\n- Run from repo root when possible.\n- Otherwise use `--project <name>` or `--path <repo-root>`.\n- List projects: `hack projects --json`.\n\n## Agent Maintenance\n\n- Project-level hack commands auto-check integration drift and attempt auto-sync.\n- Set `HACK_SETUP_SYNC_MODE=warn` to warn-only, or `HACK_SETUP_SYNC_MODE=off` to disable.\n- Refresh project + global integrations: `hack setup sync --all-scopes`\n- Check generated integrations: `hack setup sync --all-scopes --check`\n- Remove generated integrations: `hack setup sync --all-scopes --remove`\n- After self-update: `hack update` then `hack setup sync --all-scopes`\n\n## Agent Setup\n\n- Cursor rules: `hack setup cursor`\n- Claude hooks: `hack setup claude`\n- Codex skill: `hack setup codex`\n- Tickets skill: `hack setup tickets`\n- Init prompt: `hack agent init` (use --client cursor|claude|codex to open)\n- Init patterns: `hack agent patterns`\n- MCP (no shell only): `hack setup mcp`\n- MCP install (explicit): `hack mcp install --all --scope project`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:05:22.423Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Containerization Agents requiring seamless local development orchestration without port conflicts.","zh":"非常适合需要无缝本地开发编排且无端口冲突的容器化Agent。","ja":"ポート競合なしでシームレスなローカル開発オーケストレーションを必要とするコンテナ化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"포트 충돌 없이 원활한 로컬 개발 오케스트레이션이 필요한 컨테이너화 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de contenedorización que requieren una orquestación de desarrollo local sin conflictos de puertos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de conteneurisation nécessitant une orchestration de développement local sans conflits de ports.","de":"Ideal für Containerisierungsagenten, die eine reibungslose Orchestrierung der lokalen Entwicklung ohne Portkonflikte erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de containerização que requerem orquestração de desenvolvimento local perfeita sem conflitos de porta.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов контейнеризации, требующих бесшовной оркестрации локальной разработки без конфликтов портов.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء حاوية التطبيقات الذين يتطلبون أوركسترة سلسة للتطوير المحلي دون تعارض في المنافذ."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage multiple projects simultaneously using `hack` as the primary interface, leveraging `docker` and `docker compose` under the hood, while avoiding manual edits to `.hack/.internal` and `.hack/.branch` artifacts, and utilizing `hack doctor` for runtime and network repairs.","zh":"使Agent能够使用 `hack` 作为主要接口同时管理多个项目，底层利用 `docker` 和 `docker compose`，同时避免手动编辑 `.hack/.internal` 和 `.hack/.branch` 产物，并利用 `hack doctor` 进行运行时和网络修复。","ja":"主要インターフェースとして `hack` を使用して複数のプロジェクトを同時に管理するエージェントを強化し、内部で `docker` と `docker compose` を活用し、`.hack/.internal` および `.hack/.branch` 成果物の手動編集を回避し、ランタイムおよびネットワーク修復に `hack doctor` を利用します。","ko":"주요 인터페이스로 `hack`을 사용하여 여러 프로젝트를 동시에 관리하는 에이전트를 강화하며, 내부적으로 `docker` 및 `docker compose`를 활용하고, `.hack/.internal` 및 `.hack/.branch` 아티팩트를 수동으로 편집하지 않으며, 런타임 및 네트워크 수리에 `hack doctor`를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar múltiples proyectos simultáneamente utilizando `hack` como interfaz principal, aprovechando `docker` y `docker compose` en segundo plano, mientras evita ediciones manuales de los artefactos `.hack/.internal` y `.hack/.branch`, y utiliza `hack doctor` para reparaciones de tiempo de ejecución y red.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer plusieurs projets simultanément en utilisant `hack` comme interface principale, en exploitant `docker` et `docker compose` sous le capot, tout en évitant les modifications manuelles des artefacts `.hack/.internal` et `.hack/.branch`, et en utilisant `hack doctor` pour les réparations de runtime et de réseau.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, mehrere Projekte gleichzeitig zu verwalten, indem `hack` als primäre Schnittstelle verwendet wird, `docker` und `docker compose` im Hintergrund nutzt, während manuelle Bearbeitungen der Artefakte `.hack/.internal` und `.hack/.branch` vermieden werden und `hack doctor` für Laufzeit- und Netzwerkreparaturen verwendet wird.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a gerenciar vários projetos simultaneamente usando `hack` como interface principal, aproveitando `docker` e `docker compose` nos bastidores, evitando edições manuais de artefatos `.hack/.internal` e `.hack/.branch`, e utilizando `hack doctor` para reparos de tempo de execução e rede.","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять несколькими проектами одновременно, используя `hack` в качестве основного интерфейса, используя `docker` и `docker compose` под капотом, избегая ручного редактирования артефактов `.hack/.internal` и `.hack/.branch` и используя `hack doctor` для исправлений времени выполнения и сети.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة مشاريع متعددة في وقت واحد باستخدام `hack` كواجهة أساسية، والاستفادة من `docker` و `docker compose` في الخلفية، مع تجنب التعديلات اليدوية على القطع الأثرية `.hack/.internal` و `.hack/.branch`، واستخدام `hack doctor` لإصلاحات وقت التشغيل والشبكة."},"useCases":{"en":["Orchestrating local development for multiple projects","Resolving port conflicts between containerized services","Automating runtime and network repairs with `hack doctor`"],"zh":["编排多个项目的本地开发","解决容器化服务之间的端口冲突","使用 `hack doctor` 自动化运行时和网络修复"],"ja":["複数プロジェクトのローカル開発のオーケストレーション","コンテナ化されたサービス間のポート競合の解決","`hack doctor` を使用したランタイムおよびネットワーク修復の自動化"],"ko":["여러 프로젝트의 로컬 개발 오케스트레이션","컨테이너화된 서비스 간의 포트 충돌 해결","`hack doctor`를 사용한 런타임 및 네트워크 수리 자동화"],"es":["Orquestar el desarrollo local para varios proyectos","Resolver conflictos de puertos entre servicios contenedorizados","Automatizar reparaciones de tiempo de ejecución y red con `hack doctor`"],"fr":["Orchestrer le développement local pour plusieurs projets","Résoudre les conflits de ports entre les services conteneurisés","Automatiser les réparations de runtime et de réseau avec `hack doctor`"],"de":["Orchestrierung der lokalen Entwicklung für mehrere Projekte","Auflösung von Portkonflikten zwischen containterisierten Diensten","Automatisierung von Laufzeit- und Netzwerkreparaturen mit `hack doctor`"],"pt":["Orquestração de desenvolvimento local para múltiplos projetos","Resolução de conflitos de porta entre serviços containerizados","Automação de reparos de tempo de execução e rede com `hack doctor`"],"ru":["Оркестрация локальной разработки для нескольких проектов","Разрешение конфликтов портов между контейнеризированными сервисами","Автоматизация исправлений времени выполнения и сети с помощью `hack doctor`"],"ar":["أوركسترة التطوير المحلي لمشاريع متعددة","حل التعارضات في المنافذ بين الخدمات المعنونة","أتمتة إصلاحات وقت التشغيل والشبكة باستخدام `hack doctor`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires preference for `hack` over raw `docker` and `docker compose` commands","Restricts manual service management through Docker Desktop UI for `hack`-managed repositories","Needs careful handling of `.hack/.internal` and `.hack/.branch` files to avoid conflicts"],"zh":["需要偏好使用 `hack` 而非原始的 `docker` 和 `docker compose` 命令","限制通过 Docker Desktop UI 对 `hack` 管理的仓库进行手动服务管理","需要小心处理 `.hack/.internal` 和 `.hack/.branch` 文件以避免冲突"],"ja":["生の `docker` および `docker compose` コマンドよりも `hack` を優先する必要がある","`hack` が管理するリポジトリに対する Docker Desktop UI を介した手動サービス管理を制限する","競合を避けるために `.hack/.internal` および `.hack/.branch` ファイルの慎重な取り扱いが必要"],"ko":["원시 `docker` 및 `docker compose` 명령어보다 `hack` 선호가 필요함","`hack`이 관리하는 저장소에 대한 Docker Desktop UI를 통한 수동 서비스 관리 제한","충돌을 피하기 위해 `.hack/.internal` 및 `.hack/.branch` 파일을 주의해서 처리해야 함"],"es":["Requiere preferencia por `hack` sobre comandos `docker` y `docker compose` brutos","Restringe la gestión manual de servicios a través de la interfaz de usuario de Docker Desktop para los repositorios administrados por `hack`","Necesita un manejo cuidadoso de los archivos `.hack/.internal` y `.hack/.branch` para evitar conflictos"],"fr":["Nécessite une préférence pour `hack` par rapport aux commandes `docker` et `docker compose` brutes","Restreint la gestion manuelle des services via l''interface utilisateur de Docker Desktop pour les référentiels gérés par `hack`","Nécessite une manipulation soigneuse des fichiers `.hack/.internal` et `.hack/.branch` pour éviter les conflits"],"de":["Erfordert eine Präferenz für `hack` gegenüber rohen `docker`- und `docker compose`-Befehlen","Beschränkt die manuelle Dienstverwaltung über die Docker-Desktop-Benutzeroberfläche für von `hack` verwaltete Repositorys","Benötigt eine sorgfältige Handhabung der Dateien `.hack/.internal` und `.hack/.branch`, um Konflikte zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Requer preferência por `hack` em vez de comandos brutos de `docker` e `docker compose`","Restringe o gerenciamento manual de serviços através da UI do Docker Desktop para repositórios gerenciados por `hack`","Requer manipulação cuidadosa dos arquivos `.hack/.internal` e `.hack/.branch` para evitar conflitos"],"ru":["Требует предпочтения `hack` вместо сырых команд `docker` и `docker compose`","Ограничивает ручное управление сервисами через Docker Desktop UI для репозиториев, управляемых `hack`","Требует осторожного обращения с файлами `.hack/.internal` и `.hack/.branch` во избежание конфликтов"],"ar":["يتطلب تفضيل `hack` على أوامر `docker` و `docker compose` الخام","يقيد الإدارة اليدوية للخدمات عبر واجهة مستخدم Docker Desktop للمستودعات المدارة بـ `hack`","يتطلب التعامل بحذر مع ملفات `.hack/.internal` و `.hack/.branch` لتجنب التعارضات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"14aa38fb0747528de111e45fd1d094729ec60bcf46a445aebca3597e17a6e8b0","qualityScore":29}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kindfi-org/kindfi/stellar-dev', 'community', 'kindfi-org', 'kindfi', 'kindfi-org/kindfi', 'stellar-dev', 0, 0, 29, '2026-03-02T01:56:11.008Z', '2026-03-02T03:07:55.589Z', 'b8dcd872cda86918f9dd42ff0e482f8a7631c3d9948db2a8b3cba2d6f3156b3f', '{"id":"kindfi-org/kindfi/stellar-dev","name":"stellar-dev","description":{"zh":"stellar-dev是基于Stellar的开源Web3众筹平台，具有里程碑式的托管、游戏化的互动和LLM工具","ja":"stellar-devはStellarベースのオープンソースWeb3クラウドファンディングプラットフォームで、里程碑ベースのエスクロー、ゲーム化されたエンゲージメント、LLMツールを備えています","ko":"stellar-dev는 스텔라 기반의 오픈소스 Web3 크라우드펀딩 플랫폼으로, 마일스톤 기반의 에스크로, 게임화된 상호작용 및 LLM 툴을 제공","es":"stellar-dev es una plataforma de crowdfunding Web3 de código abierto basada en Stellar, con funcionalidades como escrows basados en hitos y herramientas de LLM","fr":"stellar-dev est une plateforme de crowdfunding Web3 open-source basée sur Stellar, avec des fonctionnalités telles que des escrows basés sur des jalons et des outils LLM","de":"stellar-dev ist eine Open-Source-Web3-Crowdfunding-Plattform basierend auf Stellar, mit Funktionen wie meilensteinbasierten Escrows und LLM-Tools","pt":"O stellar-dev é uma plataforma de financiamento coletivo Web3 baseada em Stellar, com recursos de escrow baseado em marcos e ferramentas LLM. Acesse o guia de desenvolvimento para saber mais","ru":"stellar-dev - это открытая платформа краудфандинга Web3, построенная на Stellar, с функциями эскроу на основе вех и инструментами LLM. Посетите гид разработчика, чтобы узнать больше","ar":"stellar-dev هي منصة تمويل جماعي مفتوحة المصدر على الويب 3 مبنية على Stellar، مع ميزات إسكرو مدمجة و أدوات LLM. زور دليل التطوير لمزيد من المعلومات","en":"KindFi is an open-source Web3 crowdfunding platform built on Stellar. Featuring milestone-based escrows, gamified engagement, and LLM tools. GUIDE: https://kindfis-organization.gitbook.io/development"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"stellar-dev AIエージェント：基于Stellar的Web3众筹平台","ja":"stellar-dev AIエージェント：StellarベースのWeb3クラウドファンディングプラットフォーム","ko":"stellar-dev AI 에이전트: 스텔라 기반 Web3 크라우드펀딩 플랫폼","es":"stellar-dev: Herramientas de Inteligencia Artificial para...","fr":"stellar-dev: Outils d''Intelligence Artificielle pour Déve...","de":"stellar-dev: KI-Tools für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: stellar-dev para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: stellar-dev для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: stellar-dev للמطورين","en":"stellar-dev"},"description":{"zh":"stellar-dev是基于Stellar的开源Web3众筹平台，具有里程碑式的托管、游戏化的互动和LLM工具","ja":"stellar-devはStellarベースのオープンソースWeb3クラウドファンディングプラットフォームで、里程碑ベースのエスクロー、ゲーム化されたエンゲージメント、LLMツールを備えています","ko":"stellar-dev는 스텔라 기반의 오픈소스 Web3 크라우드펀딩 플랫폼으로, 마일스톤 기반의 에스크로, 게임화된 상호작용 및 LLM 툴을 제공","es":"stellar-dev es una plataforma de crowdfunding Web3 de código abierto basada en Stellar, con funcionalidades como escrows basados en hitos y herramientas de LLM","fr":"stellar-dev est une plateforme de crowdfunding Web3 open-source basée sur Stellar, avec des fonctionnalités telles que des escrows basés sur des jalons et de...","de":"stellar-dev ist eine Open-Source-Web3-Crowdfunding-Plattform basierend auf Stellar, mit Funktionen wie meilensteinbasierten Escrows und LLM-Tools","pt":"O stellar-dev é uma plataforma de financiamento coletivo Web3 baseada em Stellar, com recursos de escrow baseado em marcos e ferramentas LLM. Acesse o guia d...","ru":"stellar-dev - это открытая платформа краудфандинга Web3, построенная на Stellar, с функциями эскроу на основе вех и инструментами LLM. Посетите гид разработч...","ar":"stellar-dev هي منصة تمويل جماعي مفتوحة المصدر على الويب 3 مبنية على Stellar، مع ميزات إسكرو مدمجة و أدوات LLM. زور دليل التطوير لمزيد من المعلومات","en":"KindFi is an open-source Web3 crowdfunding platform built on Stellar. Featuring milestone-based escrows, gamified engagement, and LLM tools. GUIDE: https://k..."},"definition":{"en":"KindFi is an open-source Web3 crowdfunding platform built on Stellar. Featuring milestone-based escrows, gamified engagement, and LLM tools. GUIDE: https://kindfis-organization.gitbook.io/development"},"features":{"zh":["基于Stellar的Web3众筹","里程碑式的托管","游戏化的互动","LLM工具","开源平台"],"ja":["StellarベースのWeb3クラウドファンディング","里程碑ベースのエスクロー","ゲーム化されたエンゲージメント","LLMツール","オープンソースプラットフォーム"],"ko":["스텔라 기반의 Web3 크라우드펀딩","마일스톤 기반의 에스크로","게임화된 상호작용","LLM 툴","오픈소스 플랫폼"],"es":["Plataforma de crowdfunding Web3 basada en Stellar","Escrows basados en hitos","Herramientas de LLM","Código abierto","Milestone-based escrows","Gamified engagement"],"fr":["Plateforme de crowdfunding Web3 basée sur Stellar","Escrows basés sur des jalons","Outils LLM","Code open-source","Escrows basés sur des jalons","Engagement gamifié"],"de":["Web3-Crowdfunding-Plattform basierend auf Stellar","Meilensteinbasierte Escrows","LLM-Tools","Open-Source-Code","Meilensteinbasierte Escrows","Gamifiziertes Engagement"],"pt":["Plataforma de financiamento coletivo Web3","Recursos de escrow baseado em marcos","Ferramentas LLM integradas","Código aberto e personalizável","Guia de desenvolvimento detalhado"],"ru":["Открытая платформа краудфандинга Web3","Функции эскроу на основе вех","Интегрированные инструменты LLM","Открытый и настраиваемый код","Подробный гид разработчика"],"ar":["منصة تمويل جماعي مفتوحة المصدر على الويب 3","ميزات إسكرو مدمجة","أدوات LLM متكاملة","كود مفتوح و قابل للتعديل","دليل تطوير مفصل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用stellar-dev","什么是Web3众筹","stellar-dev安装","stellar-dev设置指南","stellar-dev替代品","stellar-dev vs 其他众筹平台"],"ja":["stellar-devの使い方","Web3クラウドファンディングとは","stellar-devのインストール","stellar-devのセットアップガイド","stellar-devの代替品","stellar-dev vs その他のクラウドファンディングプラットフォーム"],"ko":["stellar-dev 사용법","Web3 크라우드펀딩이란","stellar-dev 설치","stellar-dev 설정 가이드","stellar-dev 대체품","stellar-dev vs 다른 크라우드펀딩 플랫폼"],"es":["cómo utilizar stellar-dev","qué es stellar-dev","stellar-dev alternativa","stellar-dev vs otras plataformas","instalar stellar-dev","guía de configuración de stellar-dev","desarrollo de aplicaciones con stellar-dev","herramientas de inteligencia artificial para desarrolladores"],"fr":["comment utiliser stellar-dev","qu''est-ce que stellar-dev","alternative à stellar-dev","stellar-dev vs autres plateformes","installer stellar-dev","guide de configuration de stellar-dev","développement d''applications avec stellar-dev","outils d''intelligence artificielle pour les développeurs"],"de":["wie man stellar-dev verwendet","was ist stellar-dev","stellar-dev-Alternative","stellar-dev vs andere Plattformen","stellar-dev installieren","Setup-Anleitung für stellar-dev","App-Entwicklung mit stellar-dev","KI-Tools für Entwickler"],"pt":["como usar stellar-dev","o que é stellar-dev","stellar-dev alternativa","stellar-dev vs outras plataformas","instalar stellar-dev","guia de configuração do stellar-dev","desenvolvimento de aplicativos com stellar-dev","recursos de financiamento coletivo","ferramentas LLM para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать stellar-dev","что такое stellar-dev","альтернатива stellar-dev","stellar-dev vs другие платформы","установить stellar-dev","гид по настройке stellar-dev","разработка приложений с stellar-dev","возможности краудфандинга","инструменты LLM для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام stellar-dev","ما هو stellar-dev","بديل stellar-dev","stellar-dev مقابل منصات أخرى","تثبيت stellar-dev","دليل إعداد stellar-dev","تطوير التطبيقات مع stellar-dev","إمكانيات التمويل الجماعي","أدوات LLM للمطورين"]}},"owner":"kindfi-org","repo":"kindfi","repoPath":"kindfi-org/kindfi","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:11.008Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"stellar-dev","description":"End-to-end Stellar development playbook. Covers Soroban smart contracts (Rust SDK), Stellar CLI, JavaScript/Python/Go SDKs for client apps, Stellar RPC (preferred) and Horizon API (legacy), Stellar Assets vs Soroban tokens (SAC bridge), wallet integration (Freighter, Stellar Wallets Kit), smart accounts with passkeys, status-sensitive zero-knowledge proof patterns, testing strategies, security patterns, and common pitfalls. Optimized for payments, asset tokenization, DeFi, privacy-aware applications, and financial applications. Use when building on Stellar, Soroban, or working with XLM, Stellar Assets, trustlines, anchors, SEPs, ZK proofs, or the Stellar RPC/Horizon APIs.","bodyPreview":"# Stellar Development Skill (Soroban-first)\n\n## What this Skill is for\n\nUse this Skill when the user asks for:\n\n- Soroban smart contract development (Rust)\n- Stellar dApp frontend work (React / Next.js / Node.js)\n- Wallet connection + signing flows (Freighter, etc.)\n- Transaction building / sending / confirmation\n- Stellar Asset issuance and management\n- Client SDK usage (JavaScript, Python, Go, Rust)\n- Zero-knowledge proof verification (where supported by target network/protocol)\n- Privacy-pres","body":"# Stellar Development Skill (Soroban-first)\n\n## What this Skill is for\n\nUse this Skill when the user asks for:\n\n- Soroban smart contract development (Rust)\n- Stellar dApp frontend work (React / Next.js / Node.js)\n- Wallet connection + signing flows (Freighter, etc.)\n- Transaction building / sending / confirmation\n- Stellar Asset issuance and management\n- Client SDK usage (JavaScript, Python, Go, Rust)\n- Zero-knowledge proof verification (where supported by target network/protocol)\n- Privacy-preserving applications (privacy pools, confidential tokens)\n- Local testing and deployment\n- Security hardening and audit-style reviews\n\n## What this Skill is NOT for\n\n- Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, or other non-Stellar blockchain development\n- Stellar node/validator operation (see [validators docs](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/validators))\n- General Rust programming unrelated to Soroban\n- Stellar protocol governance or CAP authoring\n\n## Default stack decisions (opinionated)\n\n### 1. Smart Contracts: Soroban (Rust)\n\n- Use Soroban SDK (`soroban-sdk` crate) for all smart contract development\n- Contracts compile to WebAssembly (WASM)\n- Use `#![no_std]` - standard library not available\n- 64KB contract size limit - use release optimizations\n- Prefer Stellar Assets over custom token contracts when possible\n\n### 2. Client SDK: stellar-sdk (JavaScript) first\n\n- Use `@stellar/stellar-sdk` for browser and Node.js applications\n- Supports both Stellar RPC and legacy Horizon API\n- Full transaction building, signing, and submission\n- Soroban contract deployment and invocation\n\n### 3. API Access: Stellar RPC first (Horizon legacy-focused)\n\n- **Prefer Stellar RPC** for new projects (JSON-RPC, real-time state)\n- **Horizon API** remains available for legacy compatibility and historical-query workflows\n- RPC: 7-day history for most methods; `getLedgers` queries back to genesis (Infinite Scroll)\n- Use Hubble/Galexie for comprehensive historical data beyond RPC\n\n### 4. Token Strategy: Stellar Assets first\n\n- **Prefer Stellar Assets** (classic issuance + trustlines) for fungible tokens\n- Built-in ecosystem support (wallets, exchanges, anchors)\n- Stellar Asset Contracts (SAC) provide Soroban interoperability\n- Use custom Soroban tokens only for complex logic requirements\n\n### 5. Testing\n\n- **Local**: Use Stellar Quickstart Docker for local network\n- **Testnet**: Use Testnet with Friendbot for funding\n- **Unit tests**: Compile to native for fast iteration\n- **Integration tests**: Deploy to local/testnet\n\n### 6. Wallet Integration\n\n- **Freighter** is the primary browser wallet\n- Use Stellar Wallets Kit for multi-wallet support\n- Wallet Standard for consistent connection patterns\n\n### 7. Freshness policy\n\n- Verify volatile facts (protocol support, RPC endpoints, CAP/SEP status, SDK API changes) against official docs before asserting them as current.\n\n## Operating procedure (how to execute tasks)\n\n### 1. Classify the task layer\n\n- Smart contract layer (Soroban/Rust)\n- Client SDK/scripts layer (JS/Python/Go)\n- Frontend/wallet layer\n- Asset management layer (issuance, trustlines)\n- Testing/CI layer\n- Infrastructure (RPC/Horizon/indexing)\n\n### Quick routing\n\n- Need custom on-chain logic? → [contracts-soroban.md](contracts-soroban.md)\n- Building a frontend/dApp? → [frontend-stellar-sdk.md](frontend-stellar-sdk.md)\n- Issuing or managing tokens? → [stellar-assets.md](stellar-assets.md)\n- Zero-knowledge proofs or privacy? → [zk-proofs.md](zk-proofs.md)\n- Setting up tests/CI? → [testing.md](testing.md)\n- Querying chain data or indexing? → [api-rpc-horizon.md](api-rpc-horizon.md) (also see [Data Docs](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/data))\n- Security review? → [security.md](security.md)\n- Hit an error? → [common-pitfalls.md](common-pitfalls.md)\n- Need upgrade/factory/governance/DeFi architecture patterns? → [advanced-patterns.md](advanced-patterns.md)\n- Need SEP/CAP guidance and standards links? → [standards-reference.md](standards-reference.md)\n\n### 2. Pick the right building blocks\n\n- Contracts: Soroban Rust SDK + Stellar CLI\n- Frontend: stellar-sdk (JS) + Freighter/Wallets Kit\n- Backend: stellar-sdk (JS/Python/Go) + RPC\n- Assets: Classic operations or SAC for Soroban interop\n- Testing: Quickstart (local) or Testnet\n\n### 3. Implement with Stellar-specific correctness\n\nAlways be explicit about:\n\n- Network passphrase (Mainnet vs Testnet vs local)\n- Source account + sequence number\n- Fee + resource limits (for Soroban)\n- Authorization requirements\n- Trustline status for assets\n- Contract storage types (temporary vs persistent vs instance)\n\n### 4. Add tests\n\n- Unit tests: Native compilation with `#[test]`\n- Integration tests: Local Quickstart or Testnet\n- Contract tests: Use `Env` from soroban-sdk\n- Frontend tests: Mock wallet/RPC interactions\n\n### 5. Deliverables expectations\n\nWhen you implement changes, provide:\n\n- Exact files changed + diffs\n- Commands to install/build/test/deploy\n- Network configuration (passphrase, RPC endpoint)\n- Risk notes for signing/fees/storage/authorization\n\n## Progressive disclosure (read when needed)\n\n- Smart contracts: [contracts-soroban.md](contracts-soroban.md)\n- Frontend + wallets: [frontend-stellar-sdk.md](frontend-stellar-sdk.md)\n- Testing strategy: [testing.md](testing.md)\n- Stellar Assets: [stellar-assets.md](stellar-assets.md)\n- Zero-knowledge proofs: [zk-proofs.md](zk-proofs.md)\n- API access (RPC/Horizon): [api-rpc-horizon.md](api-rpc-horizon.md)\n- Security checklist: [security.md](security.md)\n- Common pitfalls: [common-pitfalls.md](common-pitfalls.md)\n- Advanced architecture patterns: [advanced-patterns.md](advanced-patterns.md)\n- SEP/CAP standards map: [standards-reference.md](standards-reference.md)\n- Ecosystem projects: [ecosystem.md](ecosystem.md)\n- Reference links: [resources.md](resources.md)\n\n## Keywords\n\nstellar, soroban, xlm, smart contracts, rust, wasm, webassembly, rpc, horizon,\nfreighter, stellar-sdk, soroban-sdk, stellar-cli, trustline, anchor, sep, passkey,\nsmart wallet, sac, stellar asset contract, defi, token, nft, scaffold stellar, constructor, upgrade, factory, governance, standards,\nzero-knowledge, zk, zk-snark, groth16, bn254, poseidon, pairing, privacy, confidential, noir, risc zero, privacy pool, merkle tree\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:07:55.589Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Web3-focused AI Agents requiring advanced Stellar network integration and Soroban smart contract development capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级Stellar网络集成和Soroban智能合约开发能力的Web3重点AI代理。","ja":"Web3に注力したStellarネットワークの高度な統合とSorobanスマートコントラクト開発機能を必要とするAIエージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 Stellar 네트워크 통합 및 Soroban 스마트 계약 개발 기능이 필요한 Web3 중심 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial centrados en Web3 que requieren una integración avanzada de la red Stellar y capacidades de desarrollo de contratos inteligentes Soroban.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle axés sur Web3 nécessitant une intégration avancée du réseau Stellar et des capacités de développement de contrats intelligents Soroban.","de":"Ideal für Web3-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine erweiterte Stellar-Netzwerkintegration und Soroban-Smart-Contract-Entwicklungsfähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA com foco em Web3 que exigem integração avançada de rede Stellar e capacidades de desenvolvimento de contrato inteligente Soroban.","ru":"Идеально для AI-агентов, ориентированных на Web3, требующих расширенной интеграции с сетью Stellar и возможностей разработки умных контрактов Soroban.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يركز على الويب 3 الذي يتطلب تكاملًا متقدمًا للشبكة ستيلار وقدرات تطوير عقود ذكية سوروبان."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and interact with Stellar dApps using React, Next.js, and Node.js, while leveraging Soroban for smart contract development in Rust, and facilitating wallet connections and transaction management through protocols like Freighter.","zh":"赋予代理使用React、Next.js和Node.js构建和与Stellar dApps交互的能力，同时利用Soroban进行Rust智能合约开发，并通过协议如Freighter实现钱包连接和事务管理。","ja":"React、Next.js、Node.jsを使用してStellar dAppsを構築および操作するエージェントをEmpowerし、Sorobanを使用してRustのスマートコントラクトを開発し、Freighterなどのプロトコルを介してウォレット接続とトランザクション管理を容易にします。","ko":"React, Next.js 및 Node.js를 사용하여 Stellar dApps를 구축하고 상호 작용할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하고 Soroban을 사용하여 Rust 스마트 계약을 개발하며 Freighter와 같은 프로토콜을 통해 지갑 연결 및 트랜잭션 관리를 용이하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear e interactuar con dApps de Stellar utilizando React, Next.js y Node.js, al mismo tiempo que aprovecha Soroban para el desarrollo de contratos inteligentes en Rust y facilita las conexiones de billetera y la gestión de transacciones a través de protocolos como Freighter.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et d''interagir avec des dApps Stellar en utilisant React, Next.js et Node.js, tout en exploitant Soroban pour le développement de contrats intelligents en Rust, et en facilitant les connexions de portefeuille et la gestion des transactions via des protocoles comme Freighter.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Stellar-dApps mit React, Next.js und Node.js zu erstellen und zu interagieren, während Soroban für die Entwicklung von Smart Contracts in Rust genutzt wird und die Verbindung von Wallets und die Transaktionsverwaltung durch Protokolle wie Freighter erleichtert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir e interagir com dApps Stellar usando React, Next.js e Node.js, aproveitando Soroban para desenvolvimento de contrato inteligente em Rust e facilitando conexões de carteira e gerenciamento de transações por meio de protocolos como Freighter.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и взаимодействовать с dApps Stellar, используя React, Next.js и Node.js, а также использует Soroban для разработки умных контрактов на Rust и облегчает подключения кошельков и управление транзакциями через протоколы, такие как Freighter.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على بناء وتفاعل مع تطبيقات داب ستيلار باستخدام رياكت و نيكست و نود، مع استخدام سوروبان لتطوير العقود الذكية بلغة راست، وتسهيل الاتصالات المحفظة وإدارة المعاملات من خلال بروتوكولات مثل فريتر."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing milestone-based escrows on the Stellar network","Building gamified engagement platforms with LLM tools integration","Implementing zero-knowledge proof verification for enhanced privacy and security","Creating and managing Stellar Assets with client SDKs in JavaScript, Python, Go, or Rust"],"zh":["在Stellar网络上开发基于里程碑的托管","使用LLM工具集成构建游戏化参与平台","实现零知识证明验证以增强隐私和安全","使用JavaScript、Python、Go或Rust的客户端SDK创建和管理Stellar资产"],"ja":["Stellarネットワーク上でマイルストーンベースのエスクローを開発する","LLMツールの統合を使用してゲーム化されたエンゲージメントプラットフォームを構築する","プライバシーとセキュリティの向上のためにゼロ知識証明の検証を実装する","JavaScript、Python、Go、またはRustのクライアントSDKを使用してStellar Assetを作成および管理する"],"ko":["Stellar 네트워크에서里程碑 기반의 에스크로를 개발","LLM 도구 통합을 사용하여 게임화된 참여 플랫폼을 구축","개인 정보 보호 및 보안을 강화하기 위해 제로 지식 증명을 구현","JavaScript, Python, Go 또는 Rust의 클라이언트 SDK를 사용하여 Stellar 자산을 생성 및 관리"],"es":["Desarrollar escrows basados en hitos en la red Stellar","Crear plataformas de participación gamificadas con integración de herramientas LLM","Implementar la verificación de prueba de conocimiento cero para una mayor privacidad y seguridad","Crear y gestionar activos de Stellar con SDK de cliente en JavaScript, Python, Go o Rust"],"fr":["Développer des escrows basés sur des jalons sur le réseau Stellar","Créer des plateformes d''engagement gamifiées avec une intégration d''outils LLM","Mettre en œuvre la vérification de preuve de connaissance zéro pour une plus grande confidentialité et sécurité","Créer et gérer des actifs Stellar avec des SDK de client en JavaScript, Python, Go ou Rust"],"de":["Meilenstein-basierte Escrows in dem Stellar-Netzwerk entwickeln","Gamifizierte Engagement-Plattformen mit LLM-Tools-Integration erstellen","Zero-Knowledge-Beweis-Verifizierung für verbesserte Privatsphäre und Sicherheit implementieren","Stellar-Assets mit Client-SDKs in JavaScript, Python, Go oder Rust erstellen und verwalten"],"pt":["Desenvolver escrows baseados em marcos na rede Stellar","Construir plataformas de engajamento gamificado com integração de ferramentas LLM","Implementar verificação de prova de conhecimento zero para privacidade e segurança aprimoradas","Criar e gerenciar Ativos Stellar com SDKs de cliente em JavaScript, Python, Go ou Rust"],"ru":["Разработка эскроу на основе вех в сети Stellar","Создание игровых платформ с интеграцией инструментов LLM","Реализация проверки доказательства с нулевым знанием для повышения конфиденциальности и безопасности","Создание и управление активами Stellar с помощью клиентских SDK на JavaScript, Python, Go или Rust"],"ar":["تطوير الإسكرو على أساس الحجارة الزمنية في شبكة ستيلار","بناء منصات المشاركة القائمة على الألعاب مع دمج أدوات ليم","تنفيذ التحقق من برهان المعرفة الصفري لتحسين الخصوصية والأمان","إنشاء وإدارة أصول ستيلار باستخدام SDK العميل في جافا سكريبت، بايثون، جو، أو راست"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Rust for Soroban smart contract development","Limited to Stellar network and compatible protocols","Dependent on specific client SDKs for JavaScript, Python, Go, or Rust"],"zh":["需要Rust知识来进行Soroban智能合约开发","仅限于Stellar网络和兼容协议","依赖特定的客户端SDK用于JavaScript、Python、Go或Rust"],"ja":["Sorobanスマートコントラクト開発のためにRustの知識が必要","Stellarネットワークと互換性のあるプロトコルに限定される","JavaScript、Python、Go、またはRustの特定のクライアントSDKに依存する"],"ko":["Soroban 스마트 계약 개발을 위해 Rust 지식이 필요","Stellar 네트워크 및 호환 가능한 프로토콜로 제한","JavaScript, Python, Go 또는 Rust의 특정 클라이언트 SDK에 의존"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de Rust para el desarrollo de contratos inteligentes Soroban","Limitado a la red Stellar y protocolos compatibles","Dependiente de SDK de cliente específicos para JavaScript, Python, Go o Rust"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance de Rust pour le développement de contrats intelligents Soroban","Limité au réseau Stellar et aux protocoles compatibles","Dépendant de SDK de client spécifiques pour JavaScript, Python, Go ou Rust"],"de":["Benötigt Rust-Kenntnisse für die Entwicklung von Soroban-Smart-Contracts","Begrenzt auf das Stellar-Netzwerk und kompatible Protokolle","Abhängig von spezifischen Client-SDKs für JavaScript, Python, Go oder Rust"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de Rust para desenvolvimento de contrato inteligente Soroban","Limitado à rede Stellar e protocolos compatíveis","Dependente de SDKs de cliente específicos para JavaScript, Python, Go ou Rust"],"ru":["Требует знания Rust для разработки умных контрактов Soroban","Ограничен сетью Stellar и совместимыми протоколами","Зависит от конкретных клиентских SDK для JavaScript, Python, Go или Rust"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة راست لتطوير العقود الذكية سوروبان","محدود بالشبكة ستيلار وبروتوكولات متوافقة","يعتمد على SDK العميل المحدد لجافا سكريبت، بايثون، جو، أو راست"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"b8dcd872cda86918f9dd42ff0e482f8a7631c3d9948db2a8b3cba2d6f3156b3f","qualityScore":29}');
