lugins para Fall Guys","API ASext para iniciantes"],"ru":["как использовать add-new-asext-api","что такое add-new-asext-api","альтернативы для add-new-asext-api","add-new-asext-api vs другие плагины","установка add-new-asext-api","руководство по настройке add-new-asext-api","разработка плагинов для Fall Guys","API ASext для начинающих"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام add-new-asext-api","ما هو add-new-asext-api","بديلات لملحق add-new-asext-api","add-new-asext-api مقابل ملحقات أخرى","تثبيت add-new-asext-api","دليل إعداد ملحق add-new-asext-api","تطوير ملحقات للعبة Fall Guys","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات ASext للمبتدئين"]}},"owner":"hzqst","repo":"metamod-fallguys","repoPath":"hzqst/metamod-fallguys","stars":16,"forks":5,"updatedAt":"2026-02-22T05:31:36Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"add-new-asext-api","description":"Add a new exported API function to the asext module, wrapping a private server.dll/server.so function for use by external plugins. Use when you need to expose CASDocumentation, CASDirectoryList, or other AngelScript-related private functions through the ASEXT_* API layer.","bodyPreview":"# Add New ASEXT API\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill covers the end-to-end process of adding a new exported API function to the **asext** module. It wraps a private function from `server.dll` (Windows) / `server.so` (Linux) and exposes it through the `ASEXT_*` API layer so that external plugins (e.g., fallguys, ascurl) can import and call it at runtime.\n\n**When to use**: You have identified a private function in the game server binary (via IDA Pro) that you want to make available to other metamod plugin","body":"# Add New ASEXT API\n\n## Overview\n\nThis skill covers the end-to-end process of adding a new exported API function to the **asext** module. It wraps a private function from `server.dll` (Windows) / `server.so` (Linux) and exposes it through the `ASEXT_*` API layer so that external plugins (e.g., fallguys, ascurl) can import and call it at runtime.\n\n**When to use**: You have identified a private function in the game server binary (via IDA Pro) that you want to make available to other metamod plugins through asext''s dynamic import system.\n\n**Prerequisite knowledge**: Familiarity with the [add-private-function-with-signatures](../add-private-function-with-signatures/SKILL.md) skill for IDA analysis and signature creation basics.\n\n## Files to Modify (6 files)\n\n| # | File | Purpose |\n|---|------|---------|\n| 1 | `asext/serverdef.h` | Function typedef + `PRIVATE_FUNCTION_EXTERN` |\n| 2 | `asext/signatures.h` | Windows signature, Linux signature + symbol |\n| 3 | `asext/server_hook.cpp` | `PRIVATE_FUNCTION_DEFINE` + `ASEXT_*` wrapper |\n| 4 | `asext/meta_api.cpp` | `FILL_FROM_*` calls (3 code paths) + `LOG_MESSAGE` |\n| 5 | `asext/asext.h` | `C_DLLEXPORT` declaration (internal header) |\n| 6 | `asext/include/asext_api.h` | typedef + extern + `IMPORT_ASEXT_API` + `IMPORT_ASEXT_API_DEFINE` macros |\n\nSee [asext-file-map.md](references/asext-file-map.md) for detailed file roles and layout.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Analyze Target Function and Create Signatures\n\nUse the [add-private-function-with-signatures](../add-private-function-with-signatures/SKILL.md) skill for the full IDA Pro workflow: decompile, extract bytes, craft signature with wildcards, and verify uniqueness.\n\n**Key observations to record** during IDA analysis:\n- **Return type** (void, int, etc.)\n- **Calling convention** (Windows: `__thiscall`/`__fastcall`/`__cdecl`; Linux: `__cdecl`)\n- **Parameter list** (types and count)\n- **Struct offsets** used inside the function (may differ between Windows and Linux)\n\n**Repeat for both platforms** (server.dll AND server.so) if both IDA databases are available.\n\n**For Linux 5.15**: Also record the C++ mangled symbol name (e.g. `_ZN16CASDocumentation19SetDefaultNamespaceEPKc`). If the binary is stripped (no symbols), only a signature is needed.\n\n### Step 2: Define Function Type in `asext/serverdef.h`\n\nAdd the typedef and extern declaration alongside existing `CASDocumentation_*` functions:\n\n```cpp\n// Comment describing the function and its Windows calling convention\ntypedef ReturnType (SC_SERVER_DECL *fnClassName_MethodName)(\n    ClassName *pthis, SC_SERVER_DUMMYARG ParamType1 param1, ParamType2 param2);\nPRIVATE_FUNCTION_EXTERN(ClassName_MethodName);\n```\n\n**Naming convention**: `fnClassName_MethodName` for the typedef, `ClassName_MethodName` for the macro name.\n\n**Calling convention selection**:\n- Class member functions (most cases): `SC_SERVER_DECL` + `SC_SERVER_DUMMYARG`\n- Static / free C functions: `SC_SERVER_CDECL` (no dummy arg)\n\n**If the function is also a hook target** (needs inline hook), add the `New*` declaration:\n```cpp\nReturnType SC_SERVER_DECL NewClassName_MethodName(\n    ClassName *pthis, SC_SERVER_DUMMYARG ParamType1 param1, ParamType2 param2);\n```\n\n### Step 3: Add Signatures in `asext/signatures.h`\n\nThe file has two sections separated by `#ifdef _WIN32` / `#else`.\n\n**Windows section** (inside `#ifdef _WIN32`):\n```cpp\n#define ClassName_MethodName_Signature \"\\x56\\x8B\\xF1\\x57...\"\n```\n\n**Linux section** (inside `#else`):\n```cpp\n#define ClassName_MethodName_Signature \"\\x56\\x53\\x83\\xEC\\x2A...\"\n#define ClassName_MethodName_Symbol \"_ZN<len>ClassName<len>MethodNameE<param_types>\"\n```\n\n**Placement**: Insert after the last function of the same class group (e.g., after `CASDocumentation_RegisterEnumValue` for CASDocumentation functions).\n\n**If signature is unknown for a platform**, use empty string `\"\"` as placeholder — the corresponding `FILL_FROM_*` call must be omitted from meta_api.cpp until the signature is provided.\n\n### Step 4: Define Function Pointer in `asext/server_hook.cpp`\n\n**4a. Add PRIVATE_FUNCTION_DEFINE** at the top of the file (with other defines):\n\n```cpp\nPRIVATE_FUNCTION_DEFINE(ClassName_MethodName);\n```\n\nThis expands to:\n```cpp\nfnClassName_MethodName g_pfn_ClassName_MethodName = NULL;\nfnClassName_MethodName g_call_original_ClassName_MethodName = NULL;\n```\n\n**4b. Add the ASEXT_* wrapper function** (the exported API that external plugins call):\n\n```cpp\nC_DLLEXPORT void ASEXT_MethodName(ClassName* pthis, ParamType1 param1)\n{\n    SC_SERVER_DUMMYVAR;\n    g_call_original_ClassName_MethodName(pthis, SC_SERVER_PASS_DUMMYARG param1);\n}\n```\n\n**Naming convention**: `ASEXT_MethodName` (drop the class name prefix, keep the method name).\n\n**Important**: The wrapper uses `g_call_original_*` (not `g_pfn_*`) to call through the original function pointer. For non-hooked functions, both point to the same address.\n\n### Step 5: Fill Function Pointer in `asext/meta_api.cpp`\n\nThere are **three code paths** in `Meta_Attach` that must be updated:\n\n**5a. Windows branch** (`#ifdef _WIN32`, ~line 162+):\n\n```cpp\nFILL_FROM_SIGNATURE(server, ClassName_MethodName);\n```\n\nOr if using a caller-based signature:\n```cpp\nFILL_FROM_SIGNATURED_CALLER_FROM_END(server, ClassName_MethodName, <offset>);\n```\n\n**5b. Linux 5.16+ branch** (`if (CreateInterface(\"SCServerDLL003\", nullptr))`, ~line 206+):\n\n```cpp\nFILL_FROM_SIGNATURE(server, ClassName_MethodName);\n```\n\nOr with caller-based:\n```cpp\nFILL_FROM_SIGNATURED_CALLER_FROM_START(server, ClassName_MethodName, <offset>);\n```\n\n**5c. Linux 5.15 branch** (`else`, ~line 262+):\n\n```cpp\nFILL_FROM_SYMBOL(server, ClassName_MethodName);\n```\n\n**5d. Add LOG_MESSAGE** (after `#endif`, ~line 300+):\n\n```cpp\nLOG_MESSAGE(PLID, \"ClassName_MethodName found at %p\", g_pfn_ClassName_MethodName);\n```\n\n**Placement in each block**: Insert after the last function of the same class group to maintain ordering.\n\nFor the full list of `FILL_FROM_*` macros and the caller-based signature approach, see [add-private-function-with-signatures](../add-private-function-with-signatures/SKILL.md) Step 5 and Step 5b.\n\n### Step 6: Add Declaration in `asext/asext.h`\n\nAdd the `C_DLLEXPORT` declaration for the wrapper function:\n\n```cpp\n/*\n    Must be called inside DocInitCallback\n*/\nC_DLLEXPORT void ASEXT_MethodName(ClassName* pthis, ParamType1 param1);\n```\n\n**Placement**: At the end of the file, or grouped with related functions.\n\n### Step 7: Add to Import API in `asext/include/asext_api.h`\n\nThis file is used by **external plugins** to dynamically import asext functions. Three locations must be updated:\n\n**7a. Add typedef + extern** (alongside existing ASEXT_* declarations):\n\n```cpp\n/*\n    Must be called inside DocInitCallback\n*/\ntypedef void(*fnASEXT_MethodName)(ClassName* pASDoc, ParamType1 param1);\n\nextern fnASEXT_MethodName ASEXT_MethodName;\n```\n\n**7b. Add to `IMPORT_ASEXT_API` macro** (the DLSYM import block):\n\n```cpp\nIMPORT_FUNCTION_DLSYM(asext, ASEXT_MethodName);\\\n```\n\n**7c. Add to `IMPORT_ASEXT_API_DEFINE` macro** (the definition block):\n\n```cpp\nIMPORT_FUNCTION_DEFINE(ASEXT_MethodName);\\\n```\n\nSee [import-macro-guide.md](references/import-macro-guide.md) for details on how these macros work.\n\n## Complete Example: `ASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace`\n\nBelow is the exact diff for adding `CASDocumentation::SetDefaultNamespace` support:\n\n### serverdef.h\n```cpp\ntypedef void (SC_SERVER_DECL* fnCASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace)(\n    CASDocumentation* pthis, SC_SERVER_DUMMYARG const char* ns);\nPRIVATE_FUNCTION_EXTERN(CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace);\n```\n\n### signatures.h\n```cpp\n// Windows (direct function body, __thiscall)\n#define CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace_Signature \\\n    \"\\x56\\x8B\\xF1\\x57\\x8B\\x7C\\x24\\x2A\\x57\\x8B\\x4E\\x24\\x8B\\x01\\xFF\\x90\\xB4\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x85\\xC0\\x78\\x03\\x89\\x7E\\x28\"\n\n// Linux (direct function body, cdecl)\n#define CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace_Signature \\\n    \"\\x56\\x53\\x83\\xEC\\x2A\\x8B\\x5C\\x24\\x2A\\x8B\\x74\\x24\\x2A\\x8B\\x43\\x20\\x8B\\x10\\x89\\x74\\x24\\x2A\\x89\\x04\\x24\\xFF\\x92\\xB4\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x85\\xC0\\x78\\x03\\x89\\x73\\x24\"\n\n#define CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace_Symbol \\\n    \"_ZN16CASDocumentation19SetDefaultNamespaceEPKc\"\n```\n\n### server_hook.cpp\n```cpp\nPRIVATE_FUNCTION_DEFINE(CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace);\n\nC_DLLEXPORT void ASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace(CASDocumentation* pthis, const char* ns)\n{\n    SC_SERVER_DUMMYVAR;\n    g_call_original_CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace(pthis, SC_SERVER_PASS_DUMMYARG ns);\n}\n```\n\n### meta_api.cpp\n```cpp\n// Windows\nFILL_FROM_SIGNATURE(server, CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace);\n\n// Linux 5.16+\nFILL_FROM_SIGNATURE(server, CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace);\n\n// Linux 5.15\nFILL_FROM_SYMBOL(server, CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace);\n\n// Logging\nLOG_MESSAGE(PLID, \"CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace found at %p\",\n    g_pfn_CASDocumentation_SetDefaultNamespace);\n```\n\n### asext.h\n```cpp\n/*\n    Must be called inside DocInitCallback\n*/\nC_DLLEXPORT void ASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace(CASDocumentation* pASDoc, const char* ns);\n```\n\n### asext_api.h\n```cpp\n// typedef + extern\ntypedef void(*fnASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace)(CASDocumentation* pASDoc, const char* ns);\nextern fnASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace ASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace;\n\n// In IMPORT_ASEXT_API macro\nIMPORT_FUNCTION_DLSYM(asext, ASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace);\\\n\n// In IMPORT_ASEXT_API_DEFINE macro\nIMPORT_FUNCTION_DEFINE(ASEXT_SetDefaultNamespace);\\\n```\n\n## Platform Differences to Watch\n\n| Aspect | Windows (server.dll) | Linux (server.so) |\n|--------|---------------------|-------------------|\n| Calling convention | `__thiscall` / `__fastcall` (ecx=this) | `cdecl` (this on stack) |\n| Struct offsets | May differ (e.g., `this+0x24`) | May differ (e.g., `this+0x20`) |\n| vtable offsets | Usually same across platforms | Usually same across platforms |\n| Signature source | IDA Pro on server.dll | IDA Pro on server.so |\n| Symbol availability | Never (use signatures only) | 5.15 has symbols; 5.16+ stripped |\n| Stack cleanup | `ret N` for thiscall | Caller cleans |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] **IDA Analysis**: Decompile target function on both Windows and Linux\n- [ ] **Signature Creation**: Create signatures from function bytes\n- [ ] **Signature Verification**: Verify uniqueness with `find_bytes` in IDA (one match only)\n- [ ] `asext/serverdef.h`: Add `typedef` + `PRIVATE_FUNCTION_EXTERN`\n- [ ] `asext/signatures.h`: Add Windows signature (line 5–45 `#ifdef _WIN32` block)\n- [ ] `asext/signatures.h`: Add Linux signature + symbol (line 46+ `#else` block)\n- [ ] `asext/server_hook.cpp`: Add `PRIVATE_FUNCTION_DEFINE`\n- [ ] `asext/server_hook.cpp`: Add `ASEXT_*` wrapper function with `C_DLLEXPORT`\n- [ ] `asext/meta_api.cpp`: Add `FILL_FROM_SIGNATURE` in Windows branch\n- [ ] `asext/meta_api.cpp`: Add `FILL_FROM_SIGNATURE` in Linux 5.16+ branch\n- [ ] `asext/meta_api.cpp`: Add `FILL_FROM_SYMBOL` in Linux 5.15 branch\n- [ ] `asext/meta_api.cpp`: Add `LOG_MESSAGE` after `#endif`\n- [ ] `asext/asext.h`: Add `C_DLLEXPORT` declaration\n- [ ] `asext/include/asext_api.h`: Add `typedef` + `extern` declaration\n- [ ] `asext/include/asext_api.h`: Add to `IMPORT_ASEXT_API` macro\n- [ ] `asext/include/asext_api.h`: Add to `IMPORT_ASEXT_API_DEFINE` macro\n- [ ] **Build**: Compile on both Windows and Linux\n- [ ] **Runtime**: Verify `LOG_MESSAGE` shows non-NULL address\n- [ ] **Integration**: Test calling `ASEXT_*` from an external plugin\n\n## References\n\n- [asext-file-map.md](references/asext-file-map.md) - Detailed file roles and insertion points\n- [import-macro-guide.md](references/import-macro-guide.md) - How the IMPORT macros work\n- [../add-private-function-with-signatures/SKILL.md](../add-private-function-with-signatures/SKILL.md) - Base skill for IDA analysis and signatures\n- [../add-private-function-with-signatures/references/signature-patterns.md](../add-private-function-with-signatures/references/signature-patterns.md) - Signature creation best practices\n- [../add-private-function-with-signatures/references/calling-conventions.md](../add-private-function-with-signatures/references/calling-conventions.md) - Calling convention reference\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-28T12:48:48.663Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Reverse Engineering Agents specializing in binary analysis and API extension for game server modules.","zh":"非常适合专注于二进制分析和游戏服务器模块API扩展的逆向工程Agent。","ja":"バイナリ解析とゲームサーバーモジュールのAPI拡張に特化したリバースエンジニアリングAgentに最適です。","ko":"바이너리 분석 및 게임 서버 모듈용 API 확장에 특화된 리버스 엔지니어링 Agent에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de ingeniería inversa especializados en análisis de binarios y extensión de API para módulos de servidores de juego.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de rétro-ingénierie spécialisés dans l''analyse de binaires et l''extension d''API pour les modules de serveur de jeu.","de":"Ideal für Reverse Engineering Agents, die sich auf die Analyse von Binärdateien und die API-Erweiterung für Spielserver-Module spezialisieren.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Engenharia Reversa especializados em análise binária e extensão de API para módulos de servidor de jogo.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов Обратной Разработки, специализирующихся на анализе бинарных файлов и расширении API для модулей игрового сервера.","ar":"مثالي لوكلات الهندسة العكسية المتخصصة في التحليل الثنائي وامتداد واجهة برمجة التطبيقات (API) لوحدات خادم اللعبة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to bridge private server.dll/server.so functions into the ASEXT_API layer for external plugin consumption. This provides direct access to low-level game server functionality through IDA Pro-identified private functions.","zh":"使Agent能够将私有server.dll/server.so函数桥接到ASEXT_API层，以供外部插件使用。这通过IDA Pro识别的私有函数提供了对底层游戏服务器功能的直接访问。","ja":"Agentが非公開のserver.dll/server.so関数をASEXT_APIレイヤーにブリッジし、外部プラグインで利用できるようにします。これにより、IDA Proで特定された非公開関数を介して、低レベルのゲームサーバー機能に直接アクセスできます。","ko":"Agent가 비공개 server.dll/server.so 함수를 ASEXT_API 계층으로 연결하여 외부 플러그인에서 사용할 수 있도록 합니다. 이를 통해 IDA Pro로 식별된 비공개 함수를 통해 로우레벨 게임 서버 기능에 직접 액세스할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes conectar las funciones privadas de server.dll/server.so a la capa ASEXT_API para el consumo de plugins externos. Esto proporciona acceso directo a la funcionalidad de bajo nivel del servidor de juego a través de funciones privadas identificadas con IDA Pro.","fr":"Permet aux agents de relier les fonctions privées de server.dll/server.so à la couche ASEXT_API pour une consommation par des plugins externes. Cela fournit un accès direct à la fonctionnalité de bas niveau du serveur de jeu via des fonctions privées identifiées par IDA Pro.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, private server.dll/server.so-Funktionen in die ASEXT_API-Schicht zu integrieren, um sie für externe Plugins nutzbar zu machen. Dies bietet direkten Zugriff auf Low-Level-Serverfunktionalität durch mit IDA Pro identifizierte private Funktionen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes conectem funções privadas do server.dll/server.so à camada ASEXT_API para consumo por plugins externos. Isso fornece acesso direto à funcionalidade de baixo nível do servidor do jogo por meio de funções privadas identificadas pelo IDA Pro.","ru":"Позволяет агентам связывать приватные функции server.dll/server.so со слоем ASEXT_API для использования внешними плагинами. Это обеспечивает прямой доступ к низкоуровневой функциональности игрового сервера через приватные функции, идентифицированные с помощью IDA Pro.","ar":"يمكن الوكلات من جسر وظائف server.dll/server.so الخاصة إلى طبقة ASEXT_API لاستهلاك الإضافات الخارجية. وهذا يوفر وصولاً مباشراً إلى وظائف خادم اللعبة منخفضة المستوى من خلال الوظائف الخاصة التي تم تحديدها بواسطة IDA Pro."},"useCases":{"en":["Wrapping private server.dll functions for plugin access","Extending ASEXT_API for Fall Guys map compatibility","Enabling external plugins like fallguys and ascurl to call internal server functions"],"zh":["封装私有server.dll函数以供插件访问","扩展ASEXT_API以实现Fall Guys地图兼容性","使外部插件（如fallguys和ascurl）能够调用内部服务器函数"],"ja":["プラグインアクセスのための非公開server.dll関数のラッピング","Fall Guysのマップ互換性のためのASEXT_APIの拡張","fallguysやascurlなどの外部プラグインが内部サーバー関数を呼び出せるようにする"],"ko":["플러그인 액세스를 위한 비공개 server.dll 함수 래핑","Fall Guys 맵 호환성을 위한 ASEXT_API 확장","fallguys 및 ascurl과 같은 외부 플러그인이 내부 서버 함수를 호출할 수 있도록 설정"],"es":["Encapsular funciones privadas de server.dll para acceso de plugins","Extender ASEXT_API para compatibilidad con mapas de Fall Guys","Habilitar plugins externos como fallguys y ascurl para llamar a funciones internas del servidor"],"fr":["Encapsulation des fonctions privées de server.dll pour l''accès des plugins","Extension d''ASEXT_API pour la compatibilité des cartes de Fall Guys","Activation des plugins externes comme fallguys et ascurl pour appeler des fonctions internes du serveur"],"de":["Kapseln privater server.dll-Funktionen für den Plugin-Zugriff","Erweitern der ASEXT_API für Fall Guys Map-Kompatibilität","Aktivieren externer Plugins wie fallguys und ascurl zum Aufruf interner Serverfunktionen"],"pt":["Encapsulamento de funções privadas do server.dll para acesso por plugins","Extensão da ASEXT_API para compatibilidade com mapas do Fall Guys","Habilitar plugins externos como fallguys e ascurl para chamar funções internas do servidor"],"ru":["Обработка приватных функций server.dll для доступа плагинов","Расширение ASEXT_API для совместимости с картами Fall Guys","Включение внешних плагинов, таких как fallguys и ascurl, для вызова внутренних функций сервера"],"ar":["تغليف وظائف server.dll الخاصة للوصول بواسطة الإضافات","تمديد ASEXT_API لتوافق خرائط Fall Guys","تمكين الإضافات الخارجية مثل fallguys و ascurl من استدعاء وظائف الخادم الداخلية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires IDA Pro for binary analysis","Dependent on server.dll/server.so private functions","Windows/Linux binary compatibility specific"],"zh":["需要IDA Pro进行二进制分析","依赖于server.dll/server.so的私有函数","特定于Windows/Linux二进制兼容性"],"ja":["バイナリ解析にIDA Proが必要","server.dll/server.soの非公開関数に依存","Windows/Linuxバイナリ互換性に特化"],"ko":["바이너리 분석을 위해 IDA Pro 필요","server.dll/server.so의 비공개 함수에 종속","Windows/Linux 바이너리 호환성에 특정됨"],"es":["Requiere IDA Pro para el análisis de binarios","Depende de funciones privadas de server.dll/server.so","Compatibilidad específica con binarios de Windows/Linux"],"fr":["Nécessite IDA Pro pour l''analyse de binaires","Dépend des fonctions privées de server.dll/server.so","Compatibilité spécifique avec les binaires Windows/Linux"],"de":["Erfordert IDA Pro für die Binäranalyse","Abhängig von privaten server.dll/server.so-Funktionen","Spezifische Windows/Linux-Binärkompatibilität"],"pt":["Requer IDA Pro para análise binária","Dependente de funções privadas do server.dll/server.so","Compatibilidade binária específica para Windows/Linux"],"ru":["Требуется IDA Pro для анализа бинарных файлов","Зависит от приватных функций server.dll/server.so","Совместимость с бинарными файлами конкретно для Windows/Linux"],"ar":["يتطلب IDA Pro للتحليل الثنائي","يعتمد على وظائف server.dll/server.so الخاصة","توافق ثنائي محدد لنظامي Windows/Linux"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3cd40dcdbc897502e8b45ce6327d64555b3f41667e5807ad395223408ee0b585","qualityScore":28}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('BluMintInc/eslint-custom-rules/system-documentation', 'community', 'BluMintInc', 'eslint-custom-rules', 'BluMintInc/eslint-custom-rules', 'system-documentation', 1, 1, 28, '2026-02-23T15:04:44Z', '2026-02-26T08:43:23.811Z', 'c6fc4377eb97362bfb37e0caad07d7b4d33de7340b76728f029e0384aa2d2c0e', '{"id":"BluMintInc/eslint-custom-rules/system-documentation","name":"system-documentation","description":{"zh":"BluMint的AI智能代理系统文档提供了自定义规则，帮助开发者优化开发流程","ja":"BluMintのAIエージェントシステムドキュメントはカスタムルールを提供し、開発者が開発プロセスを最適化できるようにする","ko":"BluMint의 AI 에이전트 시스템 문서는 사용자 정의 규칙을 제공하여 개발자가 개발 프로세스를 최적화할 수 있도록 도와줍니다","es":"Las reglas personalizadas para BluMint permiten una documentación del sistema más eficiente con herramientas de AI","fr":"Les règles personnalisées pour BluMint permettent une documentation du système plus efficace avec des outils d''IA","de":"Benutzerdefinierte Regeln für BluMint ermöglichen eine effizientere Systemdokumentation mit KI-Tools","pt":"A documentação de sistema permite criar regras personalizadas para uso em repositórios BluMint, melhorando a eficiência do desenvolvimento.","ru":"Система документации позволяет создавать пользовательские правила для использования в репозиториях BluMint, повышая эффективность разработки.","ar":"توثيق النظام يسمح بإنشاء قواعد مخصصة لاستخدامها في مستودعات BluMint، مما يحسن كفاءة التطوير.","en":"Custom rules for use in BluMint repositories."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理系统文档 - BluMint自定义规则","ja":"AIエージェントシステムドキュメント - BluMintカスタムルール","ko":"AI 에이전트 시스템 문서 - BluMint 사용자 정의 규칙","es":"Herramientas de AI: Reglas personalizadas para BluMint","fr":"Outils d''IA: Règles personnalisées pour BluMint","de":"KI-Tools: Benutzerdefinierte Regeln für BluMint","pt":"Documentação de Sistema para Ferramentas de IA","ru":"Документация Системы для ИИ Агентов","ar":"توثيق النظم لأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"system-documentation"},"description":{"zh":"BluMint的AI智能代理系统文档提供了自定义规则，帮助开发者优化开发流程","ja":"BluMintのAIエージェントシステムドキュメントはカスタムルールを提供し、開発者が開発プロセスを最適化できるようにする","ko":"BluMint의 AI 에이전트 시스템 문서는 사용자 정의 규칙을 제공하여 개발자가 개발 프로세스를 최적화할 수 있도록 도와줍니다","es":"Las reglas personalizadas para BluMint permiten una documentación del sistema más eficiente con herramientas de AI","fr":"Les règles personnalisées pour BluMint permettent une documentation du système plus efficace avec des outils d''IA","de":"Benutzerdefinierte Regeln für BluMint ermöglichen eine effizientere Systemdokumentation mit KI-Tools","pt":"A documentação de sistema permite criar regras personalizadas para uso em repositórios BluMint, melhorando a eficiência do desenvolvimento.","ru":"Система документации позволяет создавать пользовательские правила для использования в репозиториях BluMint, повышая эффективность разработки.","ar":"توثيق النظام يسمح بإنشاء قواعد مخصصة لاستخدامها في مستودعات BluMint، مما يحسن كفاءة التطوير.","en":"Custom rules for use in BluMint repositories."},"definition":{"en":"Custom rules for use in BluMint repositories."},"features":{"zh":["自定义规则","优化开发流程","BluMint集成","AI智能代理支持","灵活的配置选项"],"ja":["カスタムルール","開発プロセスの最適化","BluMintとの統合","AIエージェントのサポート","柔軟な設定オプション"],"ko":["사용자 정의 규칙","개발 프로세스 최적화","BluMint 통합","AI 에이전트 지원","유연한 구성 옵션"],"es":["Reglas personalizadas para BluMint","Mejora de la documentación del sistema","Integración con herramientas de AI","Compatibilidad con Node.js y CLI","Reglas definidas por el usuario"],"fr":["Règles personnalisées pour BluMint","Amélioration de la documentation du système","Intégration avec des outils d''IA","Compatibilité avec Node.js et CLI","Règles définies par l''utilisateur"],"de":["Benutzerdefinierte Regeln für BluMint","Verbesserung der Systemdokumentation","Integration mit KI-Tools","Kompatibilität mit Node.js und CLI","Benutzerdefinierte Regeln"],"pt":["Criação de regras personalizadas","Integração com repositórios BluMint","Melhoria da eficiência do desenvolvimento","Compatibilidade com Ferramentas de IA","Documentação de sistema personalizada"],"ru":["Создание пользовательских правил","Интеграция с репозиториями BluMint","Повышение эффективности разработки","Совместимость с ИИ Агентами","Пользовательская система документации"],"ar":["إنشاء قواعد مخصصة","التكامل مع مستودعات BluMint","تحسين كفاءة التطوير","التوافق مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","توثيق نظام مخصص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","BluMint","自定义规则","开发流程优化","如何使用AI智能代理","AI智能代理与BluMint比较","BluMint安装指南","AI智能代理设置教程"],"ja":["AIエージェント","BluMint","カスタムルール","開発プロセスの最適化","AIエージェントの使用方法","AIエージェントとBluMintの比較","BluMintのインストールガイド","AIエージェントの設定方法"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","BluMint","사용자 정의 규칙","개발 프로세스 최적화","AI 에이전트 사용 방법","AI 에이전트와 BluMint 비교","BluMint 설치 가이드","AI 에이전트 설정 방법"],"es":["herramientas de AI","reglas personalizadas para BluMint","documentación del sistema","cómo usar herramientas de AI","BluMint alternativa","instalación de herramientas de AI"],"fr":["outils d''IA","règles personnalisées pour BluMint","documentation du système","comment utiliser des outils d''IA","BluMint alternative","installation d''outils d''IA"],"de":["KI-Tools","benutzerdefinierte Regeln für BluMint","Systemdokumentation","wie man KI-Tools verwendet","BluMint Alternative","Installation von KI-Tools"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de IA","o que é documentação de sistema","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvimento","alternativas para BluMint","guia de instalação de ferramentas de IA","configuração de ferramentas de IA","desenvolvimento de software com ferramentas de IA"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое система документации","ИИ Агенты для разработки","альтернативы для BluMint","руководство по установке ИИ Агентов","настройка ИИ Агентов","разработка программного обеспечения с ИИ Агентами"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو توثيق النظام","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للتطوير","بدائل لمستودعات BluMint","دليل تثبيت أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","إعداد أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير البرمجيات مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"BluMintInc","repo":"eslint-custom-rules","repoPath":"BluMintInc/eslint-custom-rules","stars":1,"forks":1,"updatedAt":"2026-02-23T15:04:44Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"system-documentation","description":"Use when creating or updating SKILL.md documentation for major code systems.","bodyPreview":"## Purpose\n\nTo ensure that comprehensive documentation for major code systems (in the form of Claude Code Skills stored in `.claude/skills/`) is both created for new systems and diligently maintained for existing ones, reflecting their current state and design philosophy.\n\nA \"major code system\" is a collection of components, hooks, contexts, and utilities that serve a cohesive purpose and often span multiple files and directories, providing reusable functionality for other parts of the codebase.","body":"## Purpose\n\nTo ensure that comprehensive documentation for major code systems (in the form of Claude Code Skills stored in `.claude/skills/`) is both created for new systems and diligently maintained for existing ones, reflecting their current state and design philosophy.\n\nA \"major code system\" is a collection of components, hooks, contexts, and utilities that serve a cohesive purpose and often span multiple files and directories, providing reusable functionality for other parts of the codebase.\n\n## Part 1: Creating New Documentation Guides\n\nWhen you implement a new major code system that does not yet have a corresponding `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` documentation file, you should draft a new one.\n\n### Creation Steps\n1.  **Identify the Need**: Recognize that a new, cohesive system has been built (e.g., a new data handling paradigm, a complex UI widget family).\n2.  **Draft the Skill**: Create a new `SKILL.md` file in `.claude/skills/<skill-name>/`.\n3.  **Structure the Guide**: Follow the template below to structure the content.\n\n### Documentation Template\n```markdown\n---\nname: <skill-name>\ndescription: \"Use when...\"\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n\n# Introduction\n\n## Purpose\n[Hook the user on how this system can make their lives easier. Explain the **core insights** or paradigms that drive its design. Keep it concise but meaningful.]\n\n## Definitions\n\n*Reserve this section for vocabulary and conceptual terminology. Describe ideas, patterns, and domain-specific language that developers must understand. Do not list file names, concrete classes, or modules here—capture those in the optional **Core Components** section instead.*\n\n*   **[Key Term 1]**: [Clear, concise definition explaining what this concept means within the context of the system. Include any important relationships to other concepts. Focus on what developers need to understand to work with the system effectively.]\n\n*   **[Key Term 2]**: [Continue adding definitions for the core concepts, patterns, or architectural ideas that are central to understanding and using the system.]\n\n*   **[Additional Terms]**: [Add as many definitions as needed to cover the essential vocabulary of the system. These should be the terms that appear frequently in the codebase or are critical to understanding the system''s design.]\n\n## Core Components (Optional)\n[If the system exposes notable classes, modules, or files, document them here instead of the Definitions section. Provide brief descriptions that explain each component''s responsibility and how developers should interact with it.]\n\n## Why did we build [System Name]?\n[Discuss the key pain points or motivations that led to creating this system. What gap does it fill? How does it improve or simplify an existing process?]\n\n## How does this system make developers'' lives easier?\n[Explain the most common use cases and **practical benefits**. Focus on how to solve real-world problems with the system.]\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\npath/to/\n├── functions/**/*              # [Description of what''s in this directory]\n├── components/**/*             # [Description of what''s in this directory]\n└── ...\n```\n\n[Briefly describe **why** these directories exist or how they are logically organized.]\n\n## How to Use [System Name]\n[Provide several subsections on how to use the system, each complete with examples. Focus on **how to use the system, not on implementation details**. Start simple and progressively get more complex, introducing new concepts by their purpose.]\n\n## Critical Insights for Maintainers\n[Capture non-obvious lessons and rationale to guide future maintainers. Focus on pitfalls to avoid and why specific design choices were made.]\n\n### Major deviations from the initial plan\n[- List the most important changes from the original design and why they were made.]\n\n### Critical insights discovered\n[- Summarize the key insights that shaped the final design and usage patterns.]\n\n### Notable assumptions that proved inaccurate\n[- Call out initial assumptions that were revised and what replaced them.]\n\n### Important lessons or improvements\n[- Provide actionable advice for future changes and improvements while preserving system integrity.]\n```\n\n## Part 2: Updating Existing Documentation Guides\n\nWhen you significantly refactor or extend an existing code system that already has a `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` file, you must update the corresponding documentation.\n\n### Update Steps\n1.  **Identify Changes**: After modifying the code, review the changes.\n2.  **Update Documentation**: Edit the corresponding `SKILL.md` file to:\n    - Reflect new system behaviors and functionality.\n    - Incorporate any new paradigms, core ideas, or design philosophies introduced by the changes.\n    - Update code examples to be accurate and relevant.\n    - Adjust the purpose/motivation statements if the system''s role has evolved.\n\n## When This Rule Should Be Followed\n\n- **Creating**: Apply this rule **when a new major code system is implemented** and lacks documentation.\n- **Updating**: Apply this rule **after a code system with existing documentation has been significantly refactored or extended**. This is a mandatory step before considering the task complete, as outlined in the \"Agent Task Completion Standards\".\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n- **Use A-temporal phrasing**: Avoid time-coupled language (for example: \"now\", \"currently\", \"recently\", \"new\", \"old\", \"temporary\"); when editing documentation, do not refer to past states (e.g., avoid \"Refactored from v2 to v3\").\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:43:23.811Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring comprehensive system documentation and maintenance for major code systems within BluMint repositories.","zh":"适用于需要对 BluMint 仓库中主要代码系统进行全面系统文档和维护的代码分析代理。","ja":"BluMint リポジトリ内の主要なコード システムの包括的なシステム ドキュメントとメンテナンスを必要とするコード分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"BluMint 리포지토리 내 주요 코드 시스템에 대한 포괄적인 시스템 문서 및 유지 보수를 요구하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren documentación del sistema integral y mantenimiento para sistemas de código importantes dentro de los repositorios de BluMint.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une documentation système complète et une maintenance pour les systèmes de code majeurs au sein des référentiels BluMint.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die umfassende Systemdokumentation und Wartung für große Codesysteme innerhalb der BluMint-Repositorys benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que requerem documentação de sistema abrangente e manutenção para principais sistemas de código dentro dos repositórios BluMint.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа кода, требующих всесторонней документации системы и обслуживания для основных систем кода внутри репозиториев BluMint.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يحتاج إلى توثيق نظام شامل والصيانة للأ hệ thống رئيسية للشفرة داخل مخازن BluMint."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to maintain up-to-date documentation for complex codebases, utilizing custom rules and Claude Code Skills stored in `.claude/skills/`, ensuring design philosophy and current state accuracy through diligent maintenance and creation of new system documentation.","zh":"赋予代理维护最新文档的能力，用于复杂的代码库，利用自定义规则和存储在 `.claude/skills/` 中的 Claude Code Skills，通过勤勉的维护和创建新的系统文档，确保设计理念和当前状态的准确性。","ja":"エージェントに最新のドキュメントを維持する能力を与え、複雑なコードベースに`.claude/skills/`に格納された Claude Code Skills とカスタム ルールを使用し、精勤したメンテナンスと新しいシステム ドキュメントの作成を通じて、設計哲学と現在の状態の正確性を確保する。","ko":"에이전트가最新의 문서를 유지할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 복잡한 코드베이스에 `.claude/skills/`에 저장된 Claude Code Skills와 사용자 정의 규칙을 사용하여, 근면한 유지 보수와 새로운 시스템 문서의 생성을 통해 설계 철학과 현재 상태의 정확성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mantener la documentación actualizada para bases de código complejas, utilizando reglas personalizadas y Claude Code Skills almacenadas en `.claude/skills/`, asegurando la precisión de la filosofía de diseño y el estado actual a través de un mantenimiento y creación diligentes de nueva documentación del sistema.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir une documentation à jour pour des bases de code complexes, en utilisant des règles personnalisées et des compétences Claude Code stockées dans `.claude/skills/`, en assurant la précision de la philosophie de conception et de l''état actuel grâce à une maintenance et une création diligentielles de nouvelle documentation système.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, die Dokumentation für komplexe Codebasen auf dem neuesten Stand zu halten, indem sie benutzerdefinierte Regeln und Claude Code Skills verwenden, die in `.claude/skills/` gespeichert sind, und so die Genauigkeit der Designphilosophie und des aktuellen Zustands durch sorgfältige Wartung und Erstellung neuer Systemdokumentation sicherstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a manter a documentação atualizada para bases de código complexas, utilizando regras personalizadas e Habilidades de Código Claude armazenadas em `.claude/skills/`, garantindo a filosofia de design e a precisão do estado atual por meio da manutenção e criação de nova documentação do sistema.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поддерживать актуальную документацию для сложных баз кода, используя пользовательские правила и навыки кода Claude, хранящиеся в `.claude/skills/`, обеспечивая точность философии дизайна и текущего состояния за счет тщательного обслуживания и создания новой системной документации.","ar":"تمكين العميل من الحفاظ على توثيق محدث لأساسيات الشفرة المعقدة، باستخدام قواعد مخصصة ومهارات شفرة كلود المخزنة في `.claude/skills/`، وضمان فلسفة التصميم ودقة الحالة الحالية من خلال الصيانة والإنشاء الجيد للتوثيق الجديد للنظام."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating documentation for major code systems","Maintaining existing system documentation","Creating custom rules for BluMint repositories"],"zh":["为主要代码系统生成文档","维护现有的系统文档","为 BluMint 仓库创建自定义规则"],"ja":["主要なコード システムのドキュメントを生成する","既存のシステム ドキュメントをメンテナンスする","BluMint リポジトリ用のカスタム ルールを作成する"],"ko":["주요 코드 시스템에 대한 문서 생성","기존 시스템 문서 유지 보수","BluMint 리포지토리용 사용자 정의 규칙 생성"],"es":["Generación de documentación para sistemas de código importantes","Mantenimiento de la documentación del sistema existente","Creación de reglas personalizadas para los repositorios de BluMint"],"fr":["Génération de documentation pour les systèmes de code majeurs","Maintenance de la documentation système existante","Création de règles personnalisées pour les référentiels BluMint"],"de":["Erstellung von Dokumentationen für große Codesysteme","Wartung der bestehenden Systemdokumentation","Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Regeln für die BluMint-Repositorys"],"pt":["Geração de documentação para sistemas de código principais","Manutenção da documentação de sistema existente","Criação de regras personalizadas para repositórios BluMint"],"ru":["Генерация документации для основных систем кода","Обслуживание существующей документации системы","Создание пользовательских правил для репозиториев BluMint"],"ar":["توليد توثيق لأنظمة الشفرة الرئيسية","صيانة التوثيق الحالي للنظام","إنشاء قواعد مخصصة لمخازن BluMint"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `.claude/skills/` directory","Limited to BluMint repositories","Dependent on Claude Code Skills"],"zh":["需要访问 `.claude/skills/` 目录","仅限 BluMint 仓库","依赖于 Claude Code Skills"],"ja":["`.claude/skills/` ディレクトリへのアクセスが必要","BluMint リポジトリに限定される","Claude Code Skills 依存"],"ko":["`.claude/skills/` 디렉토리에 대한 액세스가 필요","BluMint 리포지토리에만 국한","Claude Code Skills에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso al directorio `.claude/skills/`","Limitado a los repositorios de BluMint","Dependiente de las Claude Code Skills"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès au répertoire `.claude/skills/`","Limité aux référentiels BluMint","Dépendant des compétences Claude Code"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Verzeichnis `.claude/skills/`","Begrenzt auf die BluMint-Repositorys","Abhängig von den Claude Code Skills"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao diretório `.claude/skills/`","Limitado a repositórios BluMint","Dependente de Habilidades de Código Claude"],"ru":["Требует доступа к каталогу `.claude/skills/`","Ограничен репозиториями BluMint","Зависит от навыков кода Claude"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الدليل `.claude/skills/`","محدود بمخازن BluMint","يعتمد على مهارات شفرة كلود"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c6fc4377eb97362bfb37e0caad07d7b4d33de7340b76728f029e0384aa2d2c0e","qualityScore":28}');
