トの機能を示しています","ko":"tanstack-query는 터보 리포의 예시로, shadcn과 넥스트.js를 통합하여 AI 에이전트의 기능을 보여줍니다","es":"tanstack-query es un ejemplo de Turbo Repo con shadcn y next.js para desarrolladores","fr":"tanstack-query est un exemple de Turbo Repo avec shadcn et next.js pour les développeurs","de":"tanstack-query ist ein Beispiel für ein Turbo Repo mit shadcn und next.js für Entwickler","pt":"O TanStack Query é uma ferramenta de IA para otimizar a performance da sua aplicação com Next.js","ru":"ИИ Агенты TanStack Query - это инструмент для оптимизации производительности вашего приложения с Next.js","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي TanStack Query هي أداة لتحسين أداء تطبيقك مع Next.js","en":"Example Turbo Repo with shadcn & next.js"},"definition":{"en":"Example Turbo Repo with shadcn & next.js"},"features":{"zh":["支持Turbo Repo","集成了shadcn和Next.js","示例代码可用于参考","支持AI工具的功能演示","易于集成和扩展"],"ja":["Turbo Repoをサポート","shadcnとNext.jsを統合","サンプルコードを参考にできる","AIエージェントの機能を示す","簡単に統合と拡張が可能"],"ko":["터보 리포 지원","shadcn과 넥스트.js 통합","예시 코드 참조 가능","AI 에이전트 기능示範","쉽게 통합 및 확장 가능"],"es":["Integración con shadcn","Compatibilidad con next.js","Ejemplo de Turbo Repo","Desarrollo de proyectos de inteligencia artificial","Mejora de la eficiencia en el desarrollo"],"fr":["Intégration avec shadcn","Compatibilité avec next.js","Exemple de Turbo Repo","Développement de projets d''intelligence artificielle","Amélioration de l''efficacité dans le développement"],"de":["Integration mit shadcn","Kompatibilität mit next.js","Beispiel für ein Turbo Repo","Entwicklung von KI-Projekten","Verbesserung der Effizienz in der Entwicklung"],"pt":["Otimização de performance com Next.js","Integração com React","Suporte a CLI","Exemplo de repositório Turbo","Compatibilidade com shadcn"],"ru":["Оптимизация производительности с Next.js","Интеграция с React","Поддержка CLI","Пример репозитория Turbo","Совместимость с shadcn"],"ar":["تحسين الأداء مع Next.js","التكامل مع React","دعم CLI","مثال على مستودع Turbo","التوافق مع shadcn"]},"keywords":{"zh":["tanstack-query","AI工具","Turbo Repo","Next.js","shadcn","如何使用tanstack-query","tanstack-query安装","tanstack-query设置指南"],"ja":["tanstack-query","AIエージェント","Turbo Repo","Next.js","shadcn","tanstack-queryの使い方","tanstack-queryのインストール","tanstack-queryの設定ガイド"],"ko":["tanstack-query","AI 에이전트","터보 리포","넥스트.js","shadcn","tanstack-query 사용법","tanstack-query 설치","tanstack-query 설정 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de inteligencia artificial","tanstack-query tutorial","shadcn y next.js","desarrollo de proyectos de ia","mejora de la eficiencia en el desarrollo","tanstack-query vs otras herramientas","instalación de tanstack-query"],"fr":["outils d''intelligence artificielle","tanstack-query tutoriel","shadcn et next.js","développement de projets d''ia","amélioration de l''efficacité dans le développement","tanstack-query vs autres outils","installation de tanstack-query"],"de":["ki-tools","tanstack-query anleitung","shadcn und next.js","entwicklung von ki-projekten","verbesserung der effizienz in der entwicklung","tanstack-query vs andere tools","installation von tanstack-query"],"pt":["como usar TanStack Query","o que é TanStack Query","TanStack Query vs React Query","instalar TanStack Query","guia de configuração do TanStack Query","alternativas ao TanStack Query"],"ru":["как использовать TanStack Query","что такое TanStack Query","TanStack Query vs React Query","установить TanStack Query","руководство по настройке TanStack Query","альтернативы TanStack Query"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام TanStack Query","ما هي TanStack Query","TanStack Query مقابل React Query","تثبيت TanStack Query","دليل إعداد TanStack Query","بديلات TanStack Query"]}},"owner":"jhs88","repo":"my-shadcn-app-monorepo","repoPath":"jhs88/my-shadcn-app-monorepo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:11.017Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tanstack-query","description":"","bodyPreview":"The skill is for consistently using useSuspenseQuery from TanStack Query (React\nQuery) in a standardized way across all frontend applications. Here''s the\npattern observed:\n\n## Basic Usage Pattern\n\n```javascript\nconst { data } = useSuspenseQuery({\n  queryKey: [\"query-key\", parameter1, parameter2],\n  queryFn: () => fetchFunction(parameter1, parameter2),\n});\n```\n\n## Common Examples from the Codebase\n\n1. Simple data fetching:\n\n```javascript\nconst { data: bids } = useSuspenseQuery({\n  queryKey: [\"bid","body":"The skill is for consistently using useSuspenseQuery from TanStack Query (React\nQuery) in a standardized way across all frontend applications. Here''s the\npattern observed:\n\n## Basic Usage Pattern\n\n```javascript\nconst { data } = useSuspenseQuery({\n  queryKey: [\"query-key\", parameter1, parameter2],\n  queryFn: () => fetchFunction(parameter1, parameter2),\n});\n```\n\n## Common Examples from the Codebase\n\n1. Simple data fetching:\n\n```javascript\nconst { data: bids } = useSuspenseQuery({\n  queryKey: [\"bids\", filters, type],\n  queryFn: () => fetchBids(filters, type),\n});\n```\n\n2. Specific data:\n\n```javascript\nconst { data } = useSuspenseQuery({\n  queryKey: [\"key\", id],\n  queryFn: () => fetchData(id),\n});\n```\n\n## Key Characteristics Observed\n\n1. Consistent naming: The hook result is destructured with data as the variable\n   name (e.g., const { data: w9Data } = useSuspenseQuery(...))\n2. Query key patterns:\n   - Simple strings for static queries: [\"vendors\"]\n   - Parameterized keys for dynamic queries: [\"vendor\", vendorId]\n   - Complex keys with multiple parameters: [\"bids\", filters, type]\n3. Integration with React Query utilities:\n   - Often used alongside getQueryClient for cache invalidation on both server\n     and client-side\n   - Combined with useMutation for CRUD operations\n   - Used in conjunction with error handling and loading states\n4. Error handling:\n   - Some components check for errors explicitly (like in\n     flh-traffic-module-frontend)\n   - Often combined with toast notifications for user feedback\n5. Testing patterns:\n   - Mocked in test files using vi.fn() to simulate data fetching\n   - Tests typically mock the query key and return expected data structures\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\n1. Loading data on page load: Used in component initialization to fetch required\n   data\n2. Content-specific information: Fetching data for specific records.\n3. Table/list data: Loading data for dynamic grids and tables\n\n## Best Practices Observed\n\nLooking at the existing codebase, you should also ensure that:\n\n1. Query keys are consistently structured with a predictable pattern that\n   includes the resource type and identifiers\n2. Error handling is implemented where appropriate, particularly in traffic/FLH\n   modules\n3. Integration with mutations is common - query invalidation happens after\n   mutations to keep data fresh\n4. The query is properly prefetched on the server-side in the page component (as\n   shown in `page.tsx` files):\n\n```javascript\nvoid queryClient.prefetchQuery({\n  queryKey: [\"resource\", id],\n  queryFn: () => fetchResource(id),\n});\n```\n\n5. Use the same query key pattern that''s already established in the codebase:\n   - [\"resource\", id] for resource data\n   - This maintains consistency with how other queries are handled\n\n## Key Points to Remember\n\n1. Always use proper import: Import getQueryClient() from\n   \"~/app/get-query-client\" over useSuspenseQuery from \"@tanstack/react-query\".\n2. Use consistent query keys: Follow the pattern [\"resource\", id]\n3. Error handling: The suspense query will automatically handle loading states\n   and errors\n4. Type safety: Make sure your action function returns proper data types that\n   match your expectations\n5. Integration with existing code: The modules already have a pattern of using\n   this approach, so maintain consistency\n\n# useMutation Pattern\n\nThis project uses a standardized pattern for data mutations (create, update,\ndelete operations) with TanStack Query. The pattern ensures consistent error\nhandling, loading states, and cache management.\n\n## Basic Mutation Structure\n\n```javascript\nconst { mutate: actionMutate, isPending: isActionPending } = useMutation({\n  mutationFn: (params) => actionFunction(params),\n  onSuccess: async () => {\n    // Success handling\n    toast.success(\"Success message\");\n\n    // Refresh related queries\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n      queryKey: [\"query-key\", parameter],\n    });\n\n    // Update UI state and navigate\n    setLocalState(updatedValue);\n    closeModal();\n    router.push(`/path/${parameter}`);\n  },\n  onError: (error) => {\n    // Error handling\n    console.error(\"Error:\", error);\n    toast.error(\n      error instanceof Error ? error.message : \"Generic error message\",\n    );\n    router.refresh();\n  },\n  onSettled: () => {\n    // Cleanup\n    form.reset();\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **Consistent Naming**:\n\n   - Mutation functions follow `actionMutate` pattern\n   - Loading states use descriptive names like `isCreating`, `isUpdating`\n   - Destructure from useMutation for clarity\n\n2. **Error Handling**:\n\n   - Always check `error instanceof Error` before accessing properties\n   - Provide generic fallback messages\n   - Log errors and show user-friendly notifications\n\n3. **Success Flow**:\n\n   - Toast notifications for immediate feedback\n   - Query invalidation to refresh data\n   - Local state updates as needed\n   - Navigation or modal management\n\n4. **Loading States**:\n   - Individual states per mutation\n   - Combine states for complex operations\n   - Disable UI elements during mutations\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Form Integration\n\n```javascript\n<form\n  onSubmit={(e) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    mutationMutate({ param1: value1, param2: value2 });\n  }}\n>\n  {/* Form fields */}\n  <SubmitButton disabled={isPending}>Submit</SubmitButton>\n</form>\n```\n\n### Query Invalidation\n\n```javascript\n// Single query\nawait queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: [\"resource\", id],\n});\n\n// Multiple related queries\nawait queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"resource\", id] });\nawait queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"related-data\", id] });\n```\n\n### Combined Loading States\n\n```javascript\nconst isProcessing = isCreating || isUpdating || isDeleting;\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Type Safety**: Use TypeScript interfaces for mutation parameters\n2. **Server Actions**: Use \"use server\" directive for mutation functions\n3. **Consistent Messaging**: Follow predictable error message patterns\n4. **Loading Feedback**: Disable buttons and show indicators during mutations\n5. **Form Cleanup**: Use `onSettled` for form resets and cleanup\n6. **Navigation**: Handle redirects appropriately after mutations\n\n## Custom Hooks (Optional)\n\nFor reusable mutations, extract to custom hooks:\n\n```javascript\nexport const useCreateResource = (onSuccess?: () => void) =>\n  useMutation({\n    mutationFn: createResource,\n    onSuccess: (data) => {\n      toast.success(\"Successfully created resource.\");\n      onSuccess?.();\n    },\n    onError: (error: Error) => {\n      toast.error(error.message || \"Failed to create resource\");\n    },\n  });\n```\n\n## Key Characteristics\n\n1. **Consistent Naming**:\n\n   - Mutation function: `actionMutate` (e.g., `createContactMutate`,\n     `updateContactMutate`)\n   - Loading state: `isActionPending` (e.g., `isCreating`, `isUpdating`)\n   - Destructured from useMutation for clarity\n\n2. **Error Handling**:\n\n   - Always check `error instanceof Error` before accessing `error.message`\n   - Provide generic fallback messages\n   - Log errors to console for debugging\n   - Show user-friendly toast notifications\n\n3. **Success Flow**:\n\n   - Toast notifications for immediate feedback\n   - Query invalidation to refresh related data\n   - Local state updates when needed\n   - Navigation or modal closing\n\n4. **Loading States**:\n   - Individual loading states per mutation\n   - Combined loading states for complex operations:\n     `const isPending = isCreating || isUpdating || isRemoving;`\n   - UI elements disabled during mutations\n\n## Common Examples from Codebase\n\n### Create Mutation (VendorContacts.tsx)\n\n```javascript\nconst { mutate: createContactMutate, isPending: isCreating } = useMutation({\n  mutationFn: (data: ContactFormValues) =>\n    addVendorContact(vendorId, {\n      name: data.name,\n      role: data.role,\n      phone: data.phone || \"\",\n      cellNumber: data.cellNumber || \"\",\n      email: data.email,\n      isPrimary: data.isPrimary ?? false,\n    }),\n  onSuccess: async () => {\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n      queryKey: [\"vendor-contacts\", vendorId],\n    });\n    const primaryContactCount = await countPrimaryContacts(vendorId);\n    setHasPrimaryVendorContact(primaryContactCount === 1);\n    setFormModalState(false);\n    toast.success(\"Successfully added vendor contact!\");\n    router.push(`/vendors/${vendorId}`);\n  },\n  onError: (error) => {\n    console.error(\"Error updating contact:\", error);\n    toast.error(\n      error instanceof Error ? error.message : \"Error saving contact!\",\n    );\n    router.refresh();\n  },\n  onSettled: () => form.reset(),\n});\n```\n\n### Delete Mutation Pattern\n\n```javascript\nconst { mutate: removeContactMutate, isPending: isRemoving } = useMutation({\n  mutationFn: async (contactId: string) => {\n    await removeVendorContact(contactId);\n    return contactId;\n  },\n  onSuccess: async (contactId: string) => {\n    toast.success(\"Successfully removed vendor contact!\");\n\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n      queryKey: [\"vendor-contacts\", vendorId],\n    });\n\n    const primaryContactCount = await countPrimaryContacts(vendorId);\n    setHasPrimaryVendorContact(primaryContactCount === 1);\n    router.push(`/vendors/${vendorId}`);\n  },\n  onError: (error) => {\n    console.error(\"Error removing contact:\", error);\n    toast.error(\n      error instanceof Error ? error.message : \"Failed to remove contact\",\n    );\n    router.refresh();\n  },\n  onSettled: () => setRemoveModalState(false),\n});\n```\n\n### Form Integration Pattern\n\n```javascript\n<form\n  onSubmit={(e) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    mutationMutate({ param1: value1, param2: value2 });\n  }}\n>\n  <Field>\n    <FieldContent>\n      <Textarea\n        value={notes}\n        onChange={(e) => setNotes(e.target.value)}\n        required\n        placeholder=\"Enter notes...\"\n      />\n      <DialogFooter>\n        <DialogClose asChild>\n          <Button variant=\"outline\">Close</Button>\n        </DialogClose>\n        <SubmitButton variant=\"destructive\" disabled={isPending}>\n          Submit Action\n        </SubmitButton>\n      </DialogFooter>\n    </FieldContent>\n  </Field>\n</form>\n```\n\n## Query Invalidation Patterns\n\n1. **Targeted Invalidation**: Always use specific query keys\n\n   ```javascript\n   await queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n     queryKey: [\"vendor-documents\", vendorId],\n   });\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiple Related Queries**: When mutations affect multiple data types\n\n   ```javascript\n   await queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n     queryKey: [\"vendor-documents\", vendorId],\n   });\n   await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"audit-logs\", vendorId] });\n   await queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n     queryKey: [\"vendor-document-counts\", vendorId],\n   });\n   ```\n\n3. **Sequential Operations**: Perform invalidations in order, sometimes with\n   additional async operations\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Type Safety**: Define proper TypeScript interfaces for mutation parameters\n2. **Server Actions**: All mutation functions should be server actions with \"use\n   server\" directive\n3. **Consistent Error Messages**: Use predictable error message patterns\n4. **Loading State Management**: Disable buttons and show loading indicators\n   during mutations\n5. **Form Reset**: Use `onSettled` callback to clean up form state\n6. **Navigation**: Use `router.push()` or `router.refresh()` appropriately after\n   mutations\n\n## Custom Hook Pattern (Advanced)\n\nFor reusable mutations, create custom hooks:\n\n```javascript\nexport const useCreateBid = (onSuccess?: () => void) =>\n  useMutation({\n    mutationFn: createBid,\n    onSuccess: (data) => {\n      toast.success(\"Successfully created bid.\");\n      onSuccess?.();\n    },\n    onError: (error: Error) => {\n      toast.error(error.message || \"Failed to create bid\", {\n        duration: Infinity,\n        action: {\n          label: \"Dismiss\",\n          onClick: () => console.log(\"Error was dismissed\"),\n        },\n      });\n    },\n  });\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nThe implementation in the modules follows a consistent pattern where:\n\n- Server-side prefetching is used to pre-load queries\n- Client-side getQueryClient or useSuspenseQuery is used for components that\n  need to fetch data\n- useMutation follows standardized patterns for all CRUD operations\n- Query keys follow a predictable naming convention\n- The same fetch action function is used consistently\n\nThis approach ensures proper hydration, loading states, consistent caching\nbehavior, and maintainable mutation logic across the application.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T03:10:16.503Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing standardized data fetching with React Query and TanStack Query","zh":"非常适合需要使用React Query和TanStack Query标准化数据获取的前端代理","ja":"React QueryとTanStack Queryを使用してデータ取得を標準化する必要があるフロントエンドエージェントに最適","ko":"React Query와 TanStack Query를 사용하여 데이터 가져오기를 표준화해야 하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan una recuperación de datos estandarizada con React Query y TanStack Query","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin d''une récupération de données standardisée avec React Query et TanStack Query","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die eine standardisierte Datenabfrage mit React Query und TanStack Query benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de busca de dados padronizada com React Query e TanStack Query","ru":"Идеально подходит для фронтенд-агентов, которым требуется стандартизированная выборка данных с помощью React Query и TanStack Query","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الواجهة الأمامية الذين يحتاجون إلى جلب بيانات موحدة باستخدام React Query و TanStack Query"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage data fetching with useSuspenseQuery, providing a standardized way to handle queries using queryKey and queryFn, and integrating seamlessly with libraries like next.js","zh":"赋予代理管理数据获取的能力，使用useSuspenseQuery提供标准化的查询处理方式，使用queryKey和queryFn，并与next.js等库无缝集成","ja":"エージェントがuseSuspenseQueryを使用してデータ取得を管理できるようにし、queryKeyとqueryFnを使用してクエリを標準化された方法で処理し、next.jsなどのライブラリとシームレスに統合する","ko":"에이전트가 useSuspenseQuery를 사용하여 데이터 가져오기를 관리할 수 있도록 하며, queryKey와 queryFn을 사용하여 쿼리를 표준화된 방법으로 처리하며, next.js와 같은 라이브러리와 무jez적으로 통합","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar la recuperación de datos con useSuspenseQuery, proporcionando una forma estandarizada de manejar consultas utilizando queryKey y queryFn, e integrándose de forma transparente con bibliotecas como next.js","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer la récupération de données avec useSuspenseQuery, en fournissant un moyen standardisé de gérer les requêtes en utilisant queryKey et queryFn, et en s''intégrant sans heurts avec des bibliothèques comme next.js","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Datenabfrage mit useSuspenseQuery zu verwalten, indem sie eine standardisierte Möglichkeit bieten, Abfragen mit queryKey und queryFn zu verwalten und sich nahtlos in Bibliotheken wie next.js zu integrieren","pt":"Capacita os agentes a gerenciar a busca de dados com useSuspenseQuery, fornecendo uma maneira padronizada de lidar com consultas usando queryKey e queryFn, e integrando-se perfeitamente com bibliotecas como next.js","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять выборкой данных с помощью useSuspenseQuery, предоставляя стандартизированный способ обработки запросов с использованием queryKey и queryFn, а также обеспечивая беспрерывную интеграцию с такими библиотеками, как next.js","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من إدارة جلب البيانات باستخدام useSuspenseQuery، مما يوفر طريقة موحدة للتعامل مع الاستعلامات باستخدام queryKey و queryFn، ويتكامل بسلاسة مع مكتبات مثل next.js"},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing data fetching across frontend applications","Implementing suspenseful data loading with useSuspenseQuery","Optimizing data fetching with queryKey and queryFn"],"zh":["在前端应用程序中标准化数据获取","使用useSuspenseQuery实现悬念数据加载","使用queryKey和queryFn优化数据获取"],"ja":["フロントエンドアプリケーション全体でデータ取得を標準化する","useSuspenseQueryを使用してサスペンスデータロードを実装する","queryKeyとqueryFnを使用してデータ取得を最適化する"],"ko":["프론트엔드 애플리케이션에서 데이터 가져오기를 표준화","useSuspenseQuery를 사용하여 서스펜스 데이터 로딩 구현","queryKey와 queryFn을 사용하여 데이터 가져오기 최적화"],"es":["Estandarizar la recuperación de datos en aplicaciones frontend","Implementar una carga de datos con suspense con useSuspenseQuery","Optimizar la recuperación de datos con queryKey y queryFn"],"fr":["Standardiser la récupération de données dans les applications frontend","Mettre en œuvre un chargement de données avec suspense avec useSuspenseQuery","Optimiser la récupération de données avec queryKey et queryFn"],"de":["Datenabfrage in Frontend-Anwendungen standardisieren","Implementierung einer Datenladefunktion mit useSuspenseQuery","Optimierung der Datenabfrage mit queryKey und queryFn"],"pt":["Padronização da busca de dados em aplicações frontend","Implementação de carregamento de dados com suspense usando useSuspenseQuery","Otimização da busca de dados com queryKey e queryFn"],"ru":["Стандартизация выборки данных во фронтенд-приложениях","Реализация загрузки данных с использованием suspense через useSuspenseQuery","Оптимизация выборки данных с помощью queryKey и queryFn"],"ar":["توحيد جلب البيانات عبر تطبيقات الواجهة الأمامية","تنفيذ تحميل البيانات مع suspense باستخدام useSuspenseQuery","تحسين جلب البيانات باستخدام queryKey و queryFn"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires React and TanStack Query setup","Limited to frontend applications using React Query"],"zh":["需要React和TanStack Query设置","仅限使用React Query的前端应用程序"],"ja":["ReactとTanStack Queryの設定が必要","React Queryを使用するフロントエンドアプリケーションに限定"],"ko":["React와 TanStack Query 설정이 필요","React Query를 사용하는 프론트엔드 애플리케이션에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de React y TanStack Query","Limitado a aplicaciones frontend que utilizan React Query"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de React et TanStack Query","Limité aux applications frontend utilisant React Query"],"de":["Benötigt eine Konfiguration von React und TanStack Query","Begrenzt auf Frontend-Anwendungen, die React Query verwenden"],"pt":["Requer configuração do React e TanStack Query","Limitado a aplicações frontend que usam React Query"],"ru":["Требует настройки React и TanStack Query","Ограничено фронтенд-приложениями, использующими React Query"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد React و TanStack Query","مقتصر على تطبيقات الواجهة الأمامية التي تستخدم React Query"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"238ba3d8b4b14db7563cec3a56544f3d4010dd2acaf4194a8926ec5017aeecb5","qualityScore":28}');
